00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:46.260
Well, Tom, here is your answer.
这一集最初有一个万圣节的冷开场。

276
00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:50.840
This episode originally had a Halloween cold open.
我们拍摄了它，而且它确实播出了，因为这一集是在万圣节那周播出的。

277
00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:56.440
We shot it, and it actually aired because this episode came out the week of Halloween.
仓库里有一个鬼屋，迈克尔在鬼屋里假装上吊。

278
00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:04.860
And there is a haunted house in the warehouse, and Michael fake hangs himself in the haunted house.
播出后，NBC 决定将其从所有未来的剧集中撤下。

279
00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:11.520
And after it aired, NBC decided to pull it from all future episodes.
所以这就是为什么你在简介里能看到它，但冷开场已经不在了。

280
00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:17.280
So that's why you're seeing it in your description, but the cold open is not there anymore.
它也不在 DVD 的删减片段部分。

281
00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:20.440
It's also not on the DVDs in the deleted scene section.
网上有演员们在这一集中穿着戏服的照片。

282
00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:24.600
There are photos of the cast in their costumes from this episode online.
我扮的是蜘蛛。

283
00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:25.660
I was a spider.
敏迪扮的是《第五元素》里的莉露。

284
00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.460
Mindy was Leeloo from Fifth Element.
没错，我想这一集里吉姆扮的是 Facebook，但他只是在脸上写了“书”字来代表 Facebook。

285
00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:35.260
Yeah, I think this is the one where Jim is Facebook, but he just wrote book on his face for Facebook.
确实如此。

286
00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:36.300
That's right.
但不管怎样，伙计们，这一集实际上是从吉姆的办公室开始的，迈克尔正在分享他周末的计划。

287
00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:46.380
But anyway, guys, instead, this episode opens in Jim's office, and Michael is sharing about his plans for the weekend.
是的，他要去参加一个大蒜节。

288
00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:49.940
Yeah, he's going to go to a garlic festival.
那是真实存在的，女士。

289
00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:52.000
It's a real thing, lady.
真的吗？

290
00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:52.960
Is it?
确实有一个波科诺大蒜与丰收节。

291
00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:56.860
There is a Pocono Garlic and Harvest Festival.
我查过了。

292
00:17:57.440 --> 00:17:58.620
I looked it up.
它每年在劳动节周末于肖尼山滑雪场举行。

293
00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:03.500
It is held every year on Labor Day weekend in the Shawnee Mountain Ski Area.
节日是在周六和周日。

294
00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.940
The festival is Saturday and Sunday.
安吉拉，我觉得我们得去一趟。

295
00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:09.120
Angela, I think we have to go.
我正要说呢。

296
00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:11.420
I was just, I was about to say it.
我知道每次你提到这类活动我都会这么说，但我告诉你，我真的很想去大蒜节。

297
00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:18.120
I know I say that every time you bring up one of these things, but I am telling you, I would love a garlic festival.
我敢打赌他们有各种用大蒜做的东西。

298
00:18:18.420 --> 00:18:21.080
I bet they have all kinds of things made from garlic.
女士，听听你的门票价格里包含了什么。

299
00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:24.200
Lady, listen to what your ticket price includes.
我等不及了。

300
00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:25.300
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

301
00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:28.880
Pages of continuous live music.
全天候不间断的现场音乐表演。

302
00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:30.180
Great.
太棒了。

303
00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:33.320
Professional chef cooking demonstrations.
专业厨师的烹饪演示。

304
00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:34.760
Ding, ding, ding.
叮，叮，叮。

305
00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:40.500
Farmer garlic growing seminars, as well as children's craft activities.
农场大蒜种植研讨会，还有儿童手工活动。

306
00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:43.060
Can adults do the craft activities?
大人可以参加手工活动吗？

307
00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:46.060
I was going to say, you got to have a craft table at a festival.
我正想说呢，节日庆典上怎么能少了手工桌。

308
00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:52.300
I found out that Pennsylvania is home to something called hardneck garlic.
我发现宾夕法尼亚州有一种叫硬颈蒜的东西。

309
00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:53.940
Hardneck garlic.
硬颈蒜。

310
00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:55.200
It's a type of garlic.
这是一种大蒜。

311
00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.460
And there are three main types of hardneck garlic.
硬颈蒜主要有三个品种。

312
00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:03.500
They are racambole, if I'm pronouncing that correctly.
如果我没读错的话，它们是乐康博大蒜。

313
00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:08.780
It has a rich, full-bodied taste, and it'll last up to six months.
它口感浓郁醇厚，保质期长达六个月。

314
00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:11.920
There's porcelain hardneck garlic.
还有瓷白硬颈蒜。

315
00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:14.380
That'll stay good up to eight months.
那种可以保存长达八个月。

316
00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:17.360
And then there's purple stripe hardneck garlic.
还有紫纹硬颈蒜。

317
00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:22.020
And it's famous for making the best baked garlic.
它以制作烤蒜的最佳原料而闻名。

318
00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:27.140
It has a distinctive bright purple streak on that papery sheath.
它的纸质外皮上有一道独特的亮紫色条纹。

319
00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:28.120
I've seen that.
我见过那种。

320
00:19:28.380 --> 00:19:32.980
Well, if you need to bake your garlic, you're going to want to buy that purple stripe garlic.
好吧，如果你需要烤大蒜，你肯定得买那种紫纹大蒜。

321
00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:33.660
Okay.
好的。

322
00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:36.380
Anyway, Michael's going to the garlic festival.
总之，迈克尔要去参加大蒜节。

323
00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:40.600
He's also very excited because there is a TCBY booth.
他非常兴奋，因为那里有个TCBY摊位。

324
00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:44.240
I remember us all going to get yogurt.
我记得我们以前经常一起去吃酸奶。

325
00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:46.160
There was this like yogurt phase.
当时好像流行过一阵酸奶热。

326
00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:48.380
I think it's still happening, obviously, right?
我觉得这种热潮显然还在持续，对吧？

327
00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:49.880
There's lots of yogurt places.
现在有很多酸奶店。

328
00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:55.280
But I feel like TCBY was the first one where we were all like, oh, my gosh, let's go get yogurt.
但我感觉TCBY是第一家让我们都惊呼“天哪，去吃酸奶吧”的店。

329
00:19:56.400 --> 00:20:02.320
No, Steve used to come to work very excited when he found a new frozen yogurt place.
不，史蒂夫以前发现新的冷冻酸奶店时，总是很兴奋地来上班。

330
00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:04.400
He was especially into it.
他特别沉迷于此。

331
00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:07.640
I feel like this line maybe came from that real-life obsession.
我觉得这句台词可能就是源于这种现实生活中的痴迷。

332
00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:09.380
It was a thing.
那确实曾是一种风潮。

333
00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:15.000
It did crack me up that Michael says, yeah, it stands for I can't believe it's yogurt.
迈克尔说TCBY代表“我不敢相信这是酸奶”（I can't believe it's yogurt），这确实把我逗乐了。

334
00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:15.740
Yeah.
是啊。

335
00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:16.740
But it's TCBY.
但其实是TCBY。

336
00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:22.860
I looked it up, Jenna, and it actually stands for the country's best yogurt.
珍娜，我查过了，它实际上代表“全国最好的酸奶”（The Country's Best Yogurt）。

337
00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:25.740
TCBY, the country's best yogurt.
TCBY，全国最好的酸奶。

338
00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:26.560
Oh.
噢。

339
00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:32.060
There used to be one in Scranton per the internet and the fashion mall, but it's no longer there.
根据互联网信息，斯克兰顿的时尚购物中心曾经有一家，但现在已经不在了。

340
00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:32.880
Huh.
哈。

341
00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:33.900
There you go.
原来如此。

342
00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:41.420
Erin is going to interrupt all of this talk of garlic and TCBY to say that Raskin Design called
艾琳打断了所有关于大蒜和TCBY的谈话，说拉斯金设计公司打来电话，

343
00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:44.220
and is expecting both of them for their meeting in an hour.
并期待他们两人一小时后去开会。

344
00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:45.180
And Jim's like, hold up.
吉姆说，等等。

345
00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:46.040
It's just me.
只有我一个人。

346
00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:49.640
Michael is delighted that they want him to tag along.
迈克尔很高兴他们想让他一起去。

347
00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:50.560
Yeah.
是啊。

348
00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:52.060
I know.
我知道。

349
00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:54.560
He's like, really?
他当时反应是，真的吗？

350
00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:56.020
Oh.
噢。

351
00:20:56.340 --> 00:20:58.020
They want me as well.
他们也想要我。

352
00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:59.340
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

353
00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:01.800
He's all like playing like he's not delighted.
他装得好像一点也不高兴似的。

354
00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:03.280
That must have been a pink card.
那一定是张粉色卡片。

355
00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:04.460
Pink card.
粉色卡片。

356
00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:05.540
Michael's delighted.
迈克尔很高兴。

357
00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:06.340
Yes.
是的。

358
00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:10.980
Well, Michael's going to try to prep Jim for this meeting.
嗯，迈克尔打算为这次会议给吉姆做些准备。

359
00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:12.580
Oh, my gosh, Jenna.
天哪，珍娜。

360
00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:16.620
In deleted scenes, this was a much bigger moment.
在删减片段里，这原本是个更重要的时刻。

361
00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:19.380
It cracked me up.
把我逗乐了。

362
00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:21.860
Michael's like, this office is very formal, Jim.
迈克尔说，吉姆，这间办公室非常正式。

363
00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:22.780
You don't just say Dave.
你不能只叫他戴夫。

364
00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:23.900
It's Mr. Borchardt.
那是博查特先生。

365
00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:25.280
And also, is that what you're wearing?
还有，你就穿成这样吗？

366
00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:31.680
And then the scene would have continued where Michael is going to help Jim retie his tie.
然后场景本应继续，迈克尔要帮吉姆重新系领带。

367
00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:33.680
He says he needs a double dimple.
他说他需要一个双酒窝。

368
00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:35.300
A double dimple.
双酒窝。

369
00:21:35.380 --> 00:21:36.420
Have you ever heard of this, Jenna?
你听说过这个吗，珍娜？

370
00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:37.080
No.
没有。

371
00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:38.280
Can we hear it?
我们能听听吗？

372
00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:40.600
Is that what you are wearing?
你就穿成这样吗？

373
00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:41.700
Yes, it is.
是的，就是这样。

374
00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:43.280
How about the knot and the tie?
那领带和领带结呢？

375
00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:43.940
Double dimple.
双酒窝。

376
00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:44.920
I think we need to go.
我想我们得走了。

377
00:21:45.100 --> 00:21:45.200
No.
不。

378
00:21:45.340 --> 00:21:45.960
Don't touch my...
别碰我的……

379
00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:48.240
You need to double dimple your tie, Jim.
吉姆，你的领带需要弄出双酒窝。

380
00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:48.820
Come on.
来吧。

381
00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:49.640
Here we go.
开始了。

382
00:21:49.860 --> 00:21:51.060
I want you to look good.
我想让你看起来体面点。

383
00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:51.680
I can't...
我不能……

384
00:21:51.680 --> 00:21:52.480
Turn around.
转过去。

385
00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:52.700
No.
不。

386
00:21:53.260 --> 00:21:53.660
Come on.
来吧。

387
00:21:53.780 --> 00:21:55.020
I can only do this in one direction.
我只能朝一个方向做这个。

388
00:21:55.140 --> 00:21:55.780
Here we go.
开始了。

389
00:21:56.740 --> 00:21:57.720
Here we go.
开始了。

390
00:21:57.860 --> 00:21:59.880
I don't want them to think that you are a country pumpkin.
我不想让他们觉得你是个乡巴佬。

391
00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:02.600
And then up through the rabbit hole.
然后穿过兔洞。

392
00:22:03.100 --> 00:22:03.460
Around.
绕过来。

393
00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:05.980
Let Mary go around.
让玛丽绕过去。

394
00:22:06.160 --> 00:22:07.460
And up again.
再绕上来。

395
00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:09.900
Through the rabbit hole.
穿过兔洞。

396
00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:11.660
And down.
然后向下。

397
00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:14.260
Into the gopher hole.
进入地鼠洞。

398
00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:15.420
Up, up, up.
向上，向上，向上。

399
00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:16.100
How do we look?
我们看起来怎么样？

400
00:22:18.680 --> 00:22:19.500
That's perfect.
太完美了。

401
00:22:21.160 --> 00:22:21.680
Okay.
好的。

402
00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:24.620
So in the scene, Michael steps behind him.
在这一幕里，迈克尔走到了他身后。

403
00:22:24.740 --> 00:22:25.920
And Jim is so annoyed.
吉姆感到非常恼火。

404
00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:28.900
He unties this tie that was really well tied.
他解开了那条原本系得很好的领带。

405
00:22:28.920 --> 00:22:31.020
He does this rabbit hole, gopher hole.
他弄了个兔子洞，地鼠洞什么的。

406
00:22:31.340 --> 00:22:35.580
He's very awkwardly trying to reach over Jim, who's taller than he is, right?
他非常笨拙地试图越过比他高的吉姆去弄，对吧？

407
00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.860
And then when he spins him around and says, how do we look?
然后当他把吉姆转过来问，我们看起来怎么样？

408
00:22:38.860 --> 00:22:40.340
He just looks...
他看起来……

409
00:22:40.340 --> 00:22:41.180
The tie looks horrible.
那领带看起来糟透了。

410
00:22:41.420 --> 00:22:43.040
Is there a double dimple now?
现在有双酒窝了吗？

411
00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:45.280
I couldn't see a double dimple.
我没看到什么双酒窝。

412
00:22:45.500 --> 00:22:47.320
And Jim's collar is all messed up.
而且吉姆的领子也弄得一团糟。

413
00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:50.380
And it's just a really physically funny scene.
这真是一个肢体动作上非常滑稽的场景。

414
00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:52.020
But it got me curious.
但这让我很好奇。

415
00:22:52.020 --> 00:22:53.460
What is a double dimple?
什么是双酒窝？

416
00:22:53.940 --> 00:22:55.400
Jenna, this is all over the internet.
珍娜，这在网上到处都是。

417
00:22:55.400 --> 00:22:58.520
It's clearly important when it comes to tying a tie.
显然这在系领带时很重要。

418
00:22:58.980 --> 00:22:59.200
What?
什么？

419
00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:01.540
Yeah, there's video tutorials.
对，还有视频教程呢。

420
00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:04.860
One says, the perfect dimple every time.
有一个视频说，每次都能系出完美的酒窝。

421
00:23:05.140 --> 00:23:08.500
There was a quote I found online that said, dimples matter.
我在网上看到一句话说，酒窝很重要。

422
00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:11.780
You'll see this even in the simplest of tie knots.
即使在最简单的领带结里你也能看到。

423
00:23:11.960 --> 00:23:13.120
The four in hand.
比如平结。

424
00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:15.720
Make sure you create the dimple under the knot.
一定要在领带结下方弄出酒窝。

425
00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:19.340
Otherwise, your tie will look flatter and less finished.
否则，你的领带看起来会很扁平，不够精致。

426
00:23:19.940 --> 00:23:20.540
Wow.
哇。

427
00:23:20.800 --> 00:23:22.140
No one wants a flat tie.
没人想要一条扁平的领带。

428
00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:23.560
You need the double dimple.
你需要双酒窝。

429
00:23:24.400 --> 00:23:25.640
I had no idea.
我完全不知道。

430
00:23:25.640 --> 00:23:30.760
Yeah, but it was a really cute scene where Michael is basically trying to get Jim all spiffy.
是啊，但那场戏真的很可爱，迈克尔基本上是想让吉姆看起来精神点。

431
00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:34.020
Well, Michael also wants him to change his watch.
嗯，迈克尔还想让他换块手表。

432
00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:36.000
He says, you need a tankard watch.
他说，你需要一块坦克表。

433
00:23:36.620 --> 00:23:37.860
I looked that up.
我查了一下。

434
00:23:38.120 --> 00:23:39.360
That's not a watch.
那根本不是表。

435
00:23:39.580 --> 00:23:40.740
There's no such thing?
没这种东西？

436
00:23:40.940 --> 00:23:42.680
There's no such thing as a tankard watch.
根本没有坦克杯表这种东西。

437
00:23:42.800 --> 00:23:45.060
There is such thing as a tank watch.
确实有坦克表（Tank watch）这种东西。

438
00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:47.560
It's a Cartier watch.
那是卡地亚的一款表。

439
00:23:47.960 --> 00:23:53.400
Apparently, it was designed after the tanks of the World War II battlefields.
据说，它的设计灵感来源于二战战场的坦克。

440
00:23:53.640 --> 00:23:55.980
It has a rectangular face.
它有一个矩形的表盘。

441
00:23:56.160 --> 00:24:03.140
