539
00:28:45.800 --> 00:28:46.600
I know.
我知道。

540
00:28:46.800 --> 00:28:47.900
It's going to be back.
它会回来的。

541
00:28:48.100 --> 00:28:48.760
It'll come back.
它会回来的。

542
00:28:48.820 --> 00:28:48.980
Don't worry.
别担心。

543
00:28:49.200 --> 00:28:50.140
It's coming back.
它会回来的。

544
00:28:50.420 --> 00:28:53.380
Pam and Andy are now chatting with the receptioniSt.
帕姆和安迪现在正在和前台接待员聊天。

545
00:28:53.380 --> 00:28:54.960
First, I watched this scene.
首先，我看了这个场景。

546
00:28:55.120 --> 00:28:58.620
I rewound it because I laughed so hard.
我倒回去又看了一遍，因为我笑得太厉害了。

547
00:28:59.420 --> 00:29:03.380
I feel like this is something I say when I'm in my mom mode.
我觉得这就像是我在“妈妈模式”下会说的话。

548
00:29:03.920 --> 00:29:06.620
Looks like someone's got a case of the definitelys.
看来某人得了“绝对症”啊。

549
00:29:08.280 --> 00:29:11.040
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

550
00:29:11.160 --> 00:29:15.500
Pam is so mortified when the receptionist thinks she's a couple with Andy.
当接待员以为她和安迪是一对时，帕姆尴尬极了。

551
00:29:15.720 --> 00:29:18.500
And she does that thing where she overcompensates, where she's like,
她总是会矫枉过正，就像这样，

552
00:29:18.740 --> 00:29:20.080
no, no, no, no, no, definitely not.
不，不，不，不，不，绝对没有。

553
00:29:20.180 --> 00:29:20.940
Definitely not.
绝对没有。

554
00:29:21.060 --> 00:29:21.820
No, no, no, no, no, no.
不，不，不，不，不，不。

555
00:29:22.540 --> 00:29:22.980
Yeah.
是啊。

556
00:29:23.140 --> 00:29:24.580
She keeps repeating it.
她一直在重复这句话。

557
00:29:24.580 --> 00:29:27.920
The receptionist was played by Jennifer Hasty.
前台接待员是由詹妮弗·黑斯蒂饰演的。

558
00:29:28.280 --> 00:29:30.000
She's been in tons of stuff.
她演过很多作品。

559
00:29:30.160 --> 00:29:34.080
She's been on Bosch, Better Call Saul, Transparent, and True Blood.
她出演过《博斯》、《风骚律师》、《透明家庭》和《真爱如血》。

560
00:29:34.380 --> 00:29:37.420
And Angela, we had the hardest time getting through this scene.
还有安吉拉，我们拍这场戏时真是费了九牛二虎之力。

561
00:29:38.200 --> 00:29:44.620
It was really difficult because they wanted me to really go on too long,
这真的很难，因为他们想让我表现得太久了，

562
00:29:44.900 --> 00:29:49.900
like way too long before Andy says somebody has a case of the definitelys.
就在安迪说某人得了“绝对症”之前，时间拖得太长了。

563
00:29:49.900 --> 00:29:58.080
The direction was like, keep hearing this idea in your head, like re-realize it over and over again.
导演的要求是，脑子里一直回响着这个念头，就像一遍又一遍地重新意识到它一样。

564
00:29:58.240 --> 00:30:01.480
So I think I do it like three times where I'm like, no, definitely not.
所以我想我大概做了三次，就是那种“不，绝对没有”。

565
00:30:02.240 --> 00:30:04.440
Oh, no, no, no, definitely not.
哦，不，不，不，绝对没有。

566
00:30:04.960 --> 00:30:08.300
It's as if she keeps saying it, but she's not saying it.
就好像她一直在说，但其实又没说出口。

567
00:30:08.500 --> 00:30:11.760
That was the direction was to keep hearing it and responding.
导演的要求就是一直听到它并做出反应。

568
00:30:11.760 --> 00:30:13.600
Well, it was really funny.
嗯，这真的很有趣。

569
00:30:13.900 --> 00:30:14.540
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

570
00:30:15.220 --> 00:30:22.500
Well, Warren and Halstead said that this plot was loosely based on a story that they heard in their real life,
沃伦和霍尔斯特德说，这个情节大致是基于他们现实生活中听到的一个故事，

571
00:30:22.620 --> 00:30:25.860
but they couldn't remember now who it was.
但他们现在记不清是谁的事了。

572
00:30:25.860 --> 00:30:32.940
But they said they had a female friend who was pregnant, and she went to Ikea with a male friend, not her husband,
但他们说他们有个怀孕的女性朋友，和一位男性朋友一起去宜家，不是她丈夫，

573
00:30:33.160 --> 00:30:36.000
and everyone kept referring to them as a couple.
结果每个人都一直把他们当成一对夫妻。

574
00:30:36.680 --> 00:30:36.760
Right.
没错。

575
00:30:36.880 --> 00:30:39.580
And they were just like, we get it.
他们当时就想，我们懂了。

576
00:30:39.700 --> 00:30:43.240
I mean, we're shopping for furniture together, and I'm pregnant.
我的意思是，我们一起买家具，而且我怀孕了。

577
00:30:43.400 --> 00:30:45.180
Everyone just kept congratulating them.
每个人都一直向他们表示祝贺。

578
00:30:45.500 --> 00:30:49.580
And so they remembered that, and that's kind of the inspiration for this plot line.
所以他们记住了这件事，这就是这个情节的灵感来源。

579
00:30:49.940 --> 00:30:53.420
And I'm sure in that moment, at first you're like, oh, actually, we're not related.
我相信在那一刻，起初你会说，哦，其实我们没关系。

580
00:30:53.560 --> 00:30:54.560
Oh, actually, we're not a couple.
哦，其实我们不是一对。

581
00:30:54.560 --> 00:30:59.700
Oh, yeah, yeah, and then at some point you're like, yeah, sure, because it's just easier to go with it.
哦，是啊，是啊，然后到某个时候你会想，好吧，随你怎么说，因为顺着话说更容易。

582
00:30:59.840 --> 00:31:01.780
You're like, we need to buy what we're buying.
你会想，我们得买我们要买的东西。

583
00:31:01.920 --> 00:31:02.240
Yeah, sure.
好吧，随你便。

584
00:31:02.480 --> 00:31:03.460
We're going to get out of there.
我们得赶紧离开那儿。

585
00:31:03.940 --> 00:31:07.060
Back at the office, Erin gets an interesting phone call.
回到办公室，艾琳接到了一个有趣的电话。

586
00:31:07.400 --> 00:31:08.200
She does.
确实。

587
00:31:08.620 --> 00:31:11.880
It's from the custodian at Raskin Design.
是拉斯金设计公司的清洁工打来的。

588
00:31:13.060 --> 00:31:16.260
Apparently, they found Michael's keys in the koi pond.
显然，他们在锦鲤池里发现了迈克尔的钥匙。

589
00:31:16.740 --> 00:31:17.180
Hmm.
嗯。

590
00:31:17.520 --> 00:31:20.000
She announces this out loud.
她大声宣布了这个消息。

591
00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:24.620
And the bullpen is an instant buzz.
办公区瞬间炸开了锅。

592
00:31:24.860 --> 00:31:25.340
Koi pond.
锦鲤池。

593
00:31:25.500 --> 00:31:26.520
Your keys in a koi pond.
你的钥匙在锦鲤池里。

594
00:31:27.080 --> 00:31:29.680
Everyone is very curious.
每个人都非常好奇。

595
00:31:30.220 --> 00:31:39.060
I love the cut to the next moment where Michael's phone rings, and then we pull out and reveal everyone hovering around reception.
我喜欢切到下一个镜头，迈克尔的电话响了，然后镜头拉开，露出每个人都围在前台周围。

596
00:31:39.060 --> 00:31:42.940
And Erin just being like, Michael, people have a lot of questions.
艾琳只是说，迈克尔，大家有很多问题要问。

597
00:31:43.400 --> 00:31:48.820
These scenes were always so much fun to film because it's just a big group clump.
这些场景拍起来总是很有趣，因为大家聚成了一大团。

598
00:31:48.820 --> 00:31:53.340
And we got to have, like, our dialogue sort of rapid fire back and forth.
我们得进行那种快速的连珠炮式的对话。

599
00:31:53.880 --> 00:31:56.520
I have such fond memories of doing scenes like that.
我对拍摄那样的场景有着非常美好的回忆。

600
00:31:57.200 --> 00:31:59.080
Well, the truth is going to come out.
嗯，真相终会大白。

601
00:31:59.760 --> 00:32:06.580
Michael tries to say, yes, he fell in a koi pond, but how do they know that he wasn't trying to save a child?
迈克尔试图解释说，没错，他是掉进了锦鲤池，但他们怎么知道他当时不是在救一个孩子呢？

602
00:32:07.500 --> 00:32:11.420
And Angela's like, so a child fell in the koi pond?
安吉拉就说，所以是有个孩子掉进锦鲤池了吗？

603
00:32:11.600 --> 00:32:13.240
And Michael's like, not yet.
迈克尔就说，还没呢。

604
00:32:14.400 --> 00:32:15.220
Not yet.
还没呢。

605
00:32:16.100 --> 00:32:17.000
It's amazing.
太绝了。

606
00:32:17.760 --> 00:32:19.440
Jim has a great talking head.
吉姆有个很棒的访谈镜头。

607
00:32:19.700 --> 00:32:24.840
He says it wasn't so much how Michael fell in, but it was how long it took him to get out.
他说重点不在于迈克尔是怎么掉进去的，而在于他爬出来花了多长时间。

608
00:32:25.340 --> 00:32:26.820
You know that's got to be true.
你知道那肯定是真的。

609
00:32:27.120 --> 00:32:30.520
You know, like, getting out of that koi pond for Warren.
你知道，就像沃伦从那个锦鲤池里爬出来一样。

610
00:32:31.100 --> 00:32:32.540
I thought the same thing.
我也这么想。

611
00:32:32.820 --> 00:32:36.480
Realizing what had happened and all the people looking over the railing at him.
意识到发生了什么，还有所有人都在栏杆上看着他。

612
00:32:37.360 --> 00:32:38.480
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

613
00:32:39.080 --> 00:32:42.680
Well, it's time for Pam and Andy to do their big pitch, right?
好了，现在是帕姆和安迪进行大推销的时候了，对吧？

614
00:32:42.880 --> 00:32:44.140
They've got their sales pitch.
他们准备了销售方案。

615
00:32:44.140 --> 00:32:48.380
Yes, they're talking to Tim Dockery, and he's really impressed.
没错，他们正在和蒂姆·多克里谈，他印象非常深刻。

616
00:32:48.380 --> 00:32:55.940
He's especially impressed, you know, because he's running a family business, and they're clearly a family business.
他特别印象深刻，因为他经营着一家家族企业，而他们显然也是一家家族企业。

617
00:32:56.280 --> 00:32:58.880
Pam and Andy have to do the, oh, no, we're not.
帕姆和安迪不得不说，哦，不，我们不是。

618
00:32:58.880 --> 00:33:00.580
But we're actually not a couple.
但我们其实不是一对。

619
00:33:01.160 --> 00:33:02.140
No, no.
不，不。

620
00:33:02.520 --> 00:33:04.780
But then Andy goes on and on.
但接着安迪就开始没完没了地说了。

621
00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:06.360
Well, it's payback time.
好吧，报应来了。

622
00:33:06.520 --> 00:33:09.600
It's payback time for the lady who had a case of the definitelys.
那个得了“绝对症”的女士，报应来了。

623
00:33:09.780 --> 00:33:10.660
I guess so.
我想是吧。

624
00:33:10.840 --> 00:33:13.740
And he says, oh, yeah, no, I'm not with her.
然后他说，哦，对，不，我没跟她在一起。

625
00:33:13.880 --> 00:33:17.840
I only date face models on a scale from one to Giselle.
我只跟长相在“一分到吉赛尔”等级之间的模特约会。

626
00:33:18.160 --> 00:33:19.460
Like, my girlfriend's a nine.
比如，我女朋友是九分。

627
00:33:20.140 --> 00:33:23.000
Pam's just a surrogate, you know, because we don't need her to look good.
帕姆只是个代用品，你知道的，因为我们不需要她长得好看。

628
00:33:23.000 --> 00:33:24.360
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

629
00:33:24.520 --> 00:33:27.520
Apparently, like, we're not a couple, but that is his baby.
显然，我们不是一对，但那是他的孩子。

630
00:33:27.720 --> 00:33:28.200
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

631
00:33:28.360 --> 00:33:29.360
He is going to claim the baby.
他打算认下这个孩子。

632
00:33:29.760 --> 00:33:29.980
Yeah.
是啊。

633
00:33:31.100 --> 00:33:31.720
All right.
好吧。

634
00:33:31.820 --> 00:33:33.820
I have two things to point out in this scene.
这一幕我有两点要指出。

635
00:33:33.960 --> 00:33:35.700
Number one is my guest star alert.
第一点是我的客串明星提醒。

636
00:33:35.900 --> 00:33:37.720
Tom Yee played Tim Dockery.
汤姆·伊饰演了蒂姆·多克里。

637
00:33:38.500 --> 00:33:42.920
According to his bio, he has lived in four countries on three continents.
根据他的个人简介，他在三个大洲的四个国家生活过。

638
00:33:43.860 --> 00:33:44.340
Impressive.
令人印象深刻。

639
00:33:44.760 --> 00:33:44.980
Yeah.
是啊。

640
00:33:44.980 --> 00:33:51.280
And he has been on The West Wing, Arrested Development, Dr. Ken, Community, and Monk.
他出演过《白宫风云》、《发展受阻》、《肯医生》、《废柴联盟》和《神探阿蒙》。

641
00:33:52.140 --> 00:33:53.420
Monk Connection.
《神探阿蒙》关联。

642
00:33:53.760 --> 00:33:54.980
We got another one of those.
我们又发现了一个。

643
00:33:54.980 --> 00:33:55.880
It's been a while.
好久没见到了。

644
00:33:56.140 --> 00:33:56.480
Yeah.
是啊。

645
00:33:56.900 --> 00:34:04.660
And then at three minutes, 55 seconds, I wanted to point out Pam's baby bump.
然后在三分五十五秒的时候，我想指出帕姆的孕肚。

646
00:34:05.520 --> 00:34:06.160
Okay.
好的。

647
00:34:06.160 --> 00:34:14.340
It is much more pronounced in this episode compared to last episode, and that is because I am wearing
和上一集相比，这一集明显大了很多，那是因为我戴了

648
00:34:14.340 --> 00:34:15.500
bump bee.
孕肚垫。

649
00:34:16.100 --> 00:34:18.300
You've gone up a size in the bump.
你的孕肚大了一号。

650
00:34:18.460 --> 00:34:19.720
I've gone up a bump.
我升级了一个孕肚。

651
00:34:20.400 --> 00:34:27.340
Alicia, our costume designer, made a document that she called the belly tracker.
我们的服装设计师艾丽西亚做了一份文档，她称之为“孕肚追踪表”。

652
00:34:28.060 --> 00:34:34.800
And she tracked from the first time we heard of Pam's pregnancy news all the way to when
她从我们第一次得知帕姆怀孕的消息开始追踪，一直到她

653
00:34:34.800 --> 00:34:41.980
she would give birth, and she painstakingly mapped out each time we needed to go up in
分娩为止，并且费尽心思地规划出我们每次需要增加

654
00:34:41.980 --> 00:34:42.420
a belly.
孕肚的时间点。

655
00:34:42.420 --> 00:34:44.680
And this was our first belly bump.
这是我们的第一个孕肚。

656
00:34:44.860 --> 00:34:45.960
We went up to bump bee.
我们用到了“孕肚B”。

657
00:34:46.500 --> 00:34:51.720
They became increasingly less comfortable, and I became increasingly more miserable.
它们变得越来越不舒服，而我也变得越来越痛苦。

658
00:34:52.060 --> 00:34:56.720
I have something to share about that later that you don't know, but I'm waiting.
关于这一点，我之后有个秘密要告诉你，但我现在先保密。

659
00:34:56.720 --> 00:34:57.660
I'm waiting.
我等着呢。

660
00:34:58.020 --> 00:34:59.300
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

661
00:34:59.580 --> 00:35:05.160
Well, Angela, I look forward to whatever this piece of information is that you will be giving
好吧，安吉拉，我很期待你之后要告诉我的

662
00:35:05.160 --> 00:35:05.740
me later.
那个消息。

663
00:35:06.040 --> 00:35:07.880
Yeah, I think it's going to make you laugh.
是啊，我觉得那会让你笑出来的。

664
00:35:08.180 --> 00:35:08.600
Okay.
好的。

665
00:35:09.140 --> 00:35:14.400
Before we leave this scene, Jenna, I wanted to share with you guys that the name Tim Dockery
在离开这个场景之前，珍娜，我想告诉你们，蒂姆·多克里这个名字

666
00:35:14.400 --> 00:35:18.880
actually came from Warren's best friend from college, who's Martin Dockery.
其实来自沃伦大学时最好的朋友，也就是马丁·多克里。

667
00:35:19.260 --> 00:35:19.880
Hi, Martin.
嗨，马丁。

668
00:35:20.200 --> 00:35:22.220
But I guess the name Martin didn't clear.
但我猜“马丁”这个名字没通过审核。

669
00:35:22.700 --> 00:35:23.780
Tim is Martin's brother.
蒂姆是马丁的兄弟。

670
00:35:24.000 --> 00:35:25.860
So there you go, Tim Dockery.
所以就这样，蒂姆·多克里。

671
00:35:25.860 --> 00:35:31.240
And it was always fun when our writers got to put a friend's name or a relative's name
每当编剧能在剧集中用上朋友或亲戚的名字时，总是很有趣。

672
00:35:31.240 --> 00:35:32.020
in an episode.
在下一场戏里有个笑话，让我笑得特别厉害。

673
00:35:32.440 --> 00:35:36.540
The next scene has a joke in it that made me laugh so hard.
我是个书呆子吗？

674
00:35:37.060 --> 00:35:38.160
Am I a dork?
迈克尔向亚伦要那种把纸夹在一起的夹子，亚伦说是订书钉。

675
00:35:39.080 --> 00:35:44.560
Michael asks Aaron for one of those clips that hold paper together, and Aaron says staples.
订书钉？

676
00:35:44.720 --> 00:35:45.220
Staples?
没错。

677
00:35:45.480 --> 00:35:45.760
Yeah.
我太喜欢这个梗了。

678
00:35:47.380 --> 00:35:48.360
I loved it.
我也是。

679
00:35:48.460 --> 00:35:49.020
I did, too.
亚伦告诉迈克尔，大卫·华莱士打电话来说，他听说迈克尔在会议上

680
00:35:49.600 --> 00:35:55.380
Aaron tells Michael that David Wallace called to say that he heard Michael made a big splash
引起了轰动。

681
00:35:55.380 --> 00:35:56.180
at the meeting.
但她随即改口，因为那并不是真的，她感到很内疚，

682
00:35:56.740 --> 00:36:00.960
But then she immediately backtracks because that didn't really happen, and she feels bad,
而且是大家怂恿她这么做的。

683
00:36:01.040 --> 00:36:02.140
and everybody put her up to it.
她说，是凯文和梅雷迪思怂恿我的。

684
00:36:02.260 --> 00:36:04.940
She says, Kevin and Meredith put me up to it.
然后凯文从文件柜后面探出头来说，我会杀了你。

685
00:36:05.040 --> 00:36:08.920
And then Kevin leans through the file cabinet and says, I will kill you.
嗯，是的，那句台词的灵感来源于现实生活中沃伦的经纪人打来电话，

686
00:36:08.920 --> 00:36:17.660
Well, but yes, that line is inspired from the real-life event when Warren's agent called
说“我听说你引起了轰动”。

687
00:36:17.660 --> 00:36:19.300
and said, I heard you made a big splash.
我们收到了一位来自安大略省的粉丝艾拉·B的提问。

688
00:36:19.300 --> 00:36:22.040
We had a fan question from Ella B.
在7分13秒时，你可以看到帕姆的电脑上有一张鱼缸的照片，那是吉姆

689
00:36:22.460 --> 00:36:23.140
in Ontario.
以前的办公桌。

690
00:36:24.010 --> 00:36:31.100
At 7 minutes, 13 seconds, you can see a picture of a fish tank on Pam's computer, which is Jim's
几秒钟后，你可以在安迪的电脑上看到同样的屏保。

691
00:36:31.100 --> 00:36:31.700
old desk.
这是在致敬锦鲤池事件吗？

692
00:36:31.860 --> 00:36:36.720
And then a couple seconds later, you can see the same screensaver on Andy's computer.
确实是。

693
00:36:37.480 --> 00:36:40.060
Was this a nod to the koi pond?
事实上，如果你仔细看迈克尔走过办公区，他注意到了安迪的电脑。

694
00:36:40.600 --> 00:36:41.520
It was.
显然，帕姆和安迪对掉进锦鲤池的事一无所知。

695
00:36:41.640 --> 00:36:46.280
And in fact, if you watch Michael walk through the bullpen, he clocks Andy's computer.
他们当时不在办公室，没法去换屏保。

696
00:36:46.980 --> 00:36:51.880
And obviously, Pam and Andy don't know anything about the falling in the koi pond.
所以我猜你得想象一下，是办公室里的某个人在搞鬼。

697
00:36:52.020 --> 00:36:54.420
They are not at the office to change their screens.
嗯，在删减片段里，很明显凯文对此玩得最开心。

698
00:36:54.780 --> 00:36:58.480
So I guess you have to imagine that someone in the office is doing this.
我不知道，通常是不是凯文那个摔倒、绊倒或者发生什么意外的人，

699
00:36:58.800 --> 00:37:04.100
Well, in the deleted scenes, it's clear that Kevin is having maybe the most fun with this.
还是说……

700
00:37:04.280 --> 00:37:08.480
I don't know if, is Kevin usually the one that falls or trips or something happens,
总之。

701
00:37:08.640 --> 00:37:10.940
and now someone else has had a big fall?
现在又有别人摔了大跟头吗？

702
00:37:10.940 --> 00:37:16.360
But in the deleted scenes, as Michael walks through the bullpen, Kevin makes this noise
但在删减片段里，当迈克尔走过办公区时，凯文发出了这种声音

703
00:37:16.360 --> 00:37:24.250
with each step, like water, like squishy water in your shoes.
每走一步都有，就像水声，就像鞋子里进了水那种黏糊糊的声音。

704
00:37:24.430 --> 00:37:25.950
And Michael's like, stop it.
迈克尔就说，别弄了。

705
00:37:26.730 --> 00:37:29.690
So someone in the office was really having fun.
所以办公室里有人真的玩得很开心。

706
00:37:30.130 --> 00:37:35.990
Well, Michael is going to hold a sensitivity training meeting in the conference room.
嗯，迈克尔要在会议室召开一场敏感度培训会议。

707
00:37:36.230 --> 00:37:36.790
Yeah.
没错。

708
00:37:37.090 --> 00:37:38.670
And we're going to make a liSt.
我们要列个清单。

709
00:37:38.670 --> 00:37:42.550
We're going to make a list of things that we can no longer talk about.
我们要列出一份以后不能再谈论的事情清单。

710
00:37:43.090 --> 00:37:44.010
No teasing.
不许取笑。

711
00:37:44.230 --> 00:37:46.190
It's called a do not mock liSt.
这叫“禁止嘲笑清单”。

712
00:37:46.850 --> 00:37:47.230
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

713
00:37:47.710 --> 00:37:50.010
Michael writes the first one, koi pond.
迈克尔写下的第一条是：锦鲤池。

714
00:37:50.190 --> 00:37:54.230
And he also admits he's fallen into the fountain at the Steamtown Mall as well.
他还承认自己也掉进过蒸汽城购物中心的喷泉里。

715
00:37:54.450 --> 00:37:56.990
So he writes koi pond and fountain.
所以他写了锦鲤池和喷泉。

716
00:37:57.490 --> 00:38:00.610
We had a fan catch from Victoria S.
我们收到了一位粉丝维多利亚·S的发现反馈，

717
00:38:00.730 --> 00:38:01.750
in Orlando, Florida.
她来自佛罗里达州奥兰多。

718
00:38:02.210 --> 00:38:06.150
When Michael says he's fallen into a fountain at the Steamtown Mall,
当迈克尔说他掉进蒸汽城购物中心的喷泉时，

719
00:38:06.150 --> 00:38:08.830
I don't think there's actually a fountain there.
我觉得那里其实根本没有喷泉。

720
00:38:09.030 --> 00:38:11.610
I was born and raised in Northeast Pennsylvania.
我在宾夕法尼亚州东北部长大。

721
00:38:11.610 --> 00:38:15.450
I have been to the Steamtown Mall, and I don't recall seeing one there.
我去过蒸汽城购物中心，我不记得那里有喷泉。

722
00:38:15.870 --> 00:38:21.170
Well, Victoria, our producer Cassie wanted to find out.
好吧，维多利亚，我们的制片人凯西想去查个究竟。

723
00:38:21.290 --> 00:38:22.570
Cassie, tell us...
凯西，告诉我们……

724
00:38:22.570 --> 00:38:22.750
What?
什么？

725
00:38:22.810 --> 00:38:25.470
What do you know about the fountain at Steamtown Mall?
关于蒸汽城购物中心的喷泉，你知道些什么？

726
00:38:25.690 --> 00:38:27.410
Do you have a deep dive, Cassie?
凯西，你深入调查了吗？

727
00:38:27.850 --> 00:38:28.370
Yes.
是的。

728
00:38:28.730 --> 00:38:34.770
I have a little deep dive of me trying to figure out if there was some fountain at the Steamtown Mall.
我做了一点深入调查，试图弄清楚蒸汽城购物中心到底有没有喷泉。

729
00:38:34.770 --> 00:38:38.710
I called and emailed, and I could not get through.
我打过电话也发过邮件，但都没联系上。

730
00:38:39.010 --> 00:38:42.510
And I think they probably were, like, super weirded out by me just saying, like,
我想他们大概觉得很奇怪，因为我只是说，

731
00:38:42.670 --> 00:38:44.890
hi, just want to know if there's a fountain here.
你好，我只是想知道这里有没有喷泉。

732
00:38:45.190 --> 00:38:47.550
So they weren't responding to me.
所以他们没回复我。

733
00:38:47.770 --> 00:38:49.190
And I, like, went on Google.
然后我上了谷歌。

734
00:38:49.230 --> 00:38:50.690
I tried to look at pictures.
我试着找照片看。

735
00:38:50.910 --> 00:38:55.130
I watched, like, old news clips of people doing segments at the mall,
我看了人们在商场做节目的旧新闻片段，

736
00:38:55.130 --> 00:38:56.590
and I could not find a fountain.
但我没找到喷泉。

737
00:38:57.010 --> 00:38:59.370
I was about to give up, and I was like, you know what?
我正要放弃的时候，我想，你知道吗？

738
00:38:59.370 --> 00:39:03.070
I'm going to reach out to the Office Ladies Facebook fan page,
我要联系“办公室女士”的Facebook粉丝专页，

739
00:39:03.210 --> 00:39:06.670
because people post, like, pictures of them in Scranton.
因为人们会发他们在斯克兰顿的照片。

740
00:39:06.970 --> 00:39:12.470
So I reached out to Nikki, who moderates it, and then she was like, I'm on it.
所以我联系了版主妮基，她当时就说，交给我吧。

741
00:39:12.590 --> 00:39:17.170
And, like, a couple hours later, she got back to me and was like,
几个小时后，她回复我说，

742
00:39:17.330 --> 00:39:18.830
so I couldn't find any pictures.
我没找到任何照片。

743
00:39:19.090 --> 00:39:22.830
I called the Steamtown Mall, got a hold of someone.
我给蒸汽城购物中心打了电话，联系上了一个人。

744
00:39:22.830 --> 00:39:27.370
They were very weirded out by her asking if there's a fountain there.
他们对她询问那里有没有喷泉感到非常困惑。

745
00:39:27.490 --> 00:39:30.830
Why are all these people calling and asking if there's a fountain?
为什么这些人都在打电话问有没有喷泉？

746
00:39:32.490 --> 00:39:32.970
Yeah.
没错。

747
00:39:33.550 --> 00:39:36.270
So they, like, were like, well, we'll get your name and phone number,
他们说，好吧，我们要记下你的姓名和电话号码，

748
00:39:36.270 --> 00:39:37.950
and someone will contact you.
会有人联系你的。

749
00:39:38.230 --> 00:39:42.210
And then an hour later, she just got a text message from them saying, no, we don't.
结果一小时后，她收到了一条短信，说没有，我们没有喷泉。

750
00:39:42.510 --> 00:39:43.210
All right.
好吧。

751
00:39:43.870 --> 00:39:45.870
I love this story so much.
我太喜欢这个故事了。

752
00:39:46.030 --> 00:39:50.370
I love that both of you women were calling the Steamtown Mall,
我喜欢你们两位女士给斯廷敦购物中心打电话，

753
00:39:50.370 --> 00:39:53.050
asking if there's a fountain, and the people are like,
问那里有没有喷泉，然后工作人员心想，

754
00:39:53.150 --> 00:39:55.530
what do these ladies want to do in a fountain?
这些女士到底想在喷泉里干什么？

755
00:39:55.770 --> 00:39:57.890
Why are they looking for a fountain so badly?
她们为什么这么急着找喷泉？

756
00:39:58.250 --> 00:40:01.890
I want to picture the person answering the phone, like, later that day.
我真想想象一下那天晚些时候接电话的那个人。

757
00:40:02.030 --> 00:40:04.430
Maybe they're on their break, you know, having a snack.
也许他们当时正在休息，你知道，吃着零食。

758
00:40:04.450 --> 00:40:06.290
They're with other co-workers, and they're like,
他们和同事在一起，然后说，

759
00:40:06.830 --> 00:40:10.330
you guys getting calls, like, with people asking if we have a fountain?
你们有没有接到那种问我们有没有喷泉的电话？

760
00:40:10.610 --> 00:40:11.530
Like, what the hell?
真是的，搞什么鬼？

761
00:40:12.890 --> 00:40:14.190
Thank you, Cassie.
谢谢你，卡西。

762
00:40:14.350 --> 00:40:16.350
But, Victoria, you are right.
但是，维多利亚，你是对的。

763
00:40:16.350 --> 00:40:18.730
There is no fountain in the Steamtown Mall.
斯廷敦购物中心确实没有喷泉。

764
00:40:19.010 --> 00:40:19.490
Yes.
是的。

765
00:40:20.410 --> 00:40:20.930
Okay.
好的。

766
00:40:21.810 --> 00:40:25.710
Well, Angela, I have a mystery I want to solve from this scene,
嗯，安吉拉，这一幕里有个我想解开的谜题，

767
00:40:26.350 --> 00:40:29.510
and I'm calling it Ryan has glasses.
我把它叫做“瑞安戴眼镜”。

768
00:40:30.410 --> 00:40:34.630
Remember last episode, he was wearing his Trilby hat?
还记得上一集吗，他戴着那顶软呢帽？

769
00:40:34.930 --> 00:40:35.050
Yes.
记得。

770
00:40:35.990 --> 00:40:38.550
Well, now he's holding a pair of glasses.
嗯，现在他手里拿着一副眼镜。

771
00:40:38.710 --> 00:40:40.070
They never go on his face.
但他从来没戴上过。

772
00:40:40.330 --> 00:40:43.010
After I saw this, I watched the whole episode,
看完这一幕后，我把整集都看完了，

773
00:40:43.230 --> 00:40:45.550
waiting for those glasses to go on his face.
就等着看他把眼镜戴上。

774
00:40:45.710 --> 00:40:47.650
But he's just gesturing with them.
但他只是拿着眼镜比划。

775
00:40:47.930 --> 00:40:48.550
What's up?
怎么回事？

776
00:40:48.550 --> 00:40:50.050
He's got a pair of fake glasses.
他拿着一副假眼镜。

777
00:40:50.290 --> 00:40:51.610
I don't know what he's going through.
我不知道他到底在搞什么。

778
00:40:51.930 --> 00:40:53.590
Ryan and the accessories.
瑞安和他的配饰。

779
00:40:53.990 --> 00:40:54.190
Yeah.
是啊。

780
00:40:54.190 --> 00:40:55.950
He's wanting to feel dignified or something.
他大概是想让自己看起来庄重一点之类的吧。

781
00:40:56.210 --> 00:40:57.250
I guess so.
我想是吧。

782
00:40:57.530 --> 00:41:00.750
Michael wants other people to shout out things they don't want to be teased about.
迈克尔想让其他人大声说出他们不想被取笑的事情。

783
00:41:01.090 --> 00:41:02.390
And Dwight volunteers.
然后德怀特主动请缨。

784
00:41:02.390 --> 00:41:05.230
He says, my nose is too small.
他说，我的鼻子太小了。

785
00:41:05.410 --> 00:41:07.450
And then he has a talking head where he says,
接着他有一个采访镜头，他说，

786
00:41:07.910 --> 00:41:11.310
the geometric proportions of my face are perfect in every way but one.
我脸部的几何比例在各方面都很完美，只有一点除外。

787
00:41:11.550 --> 00:41:13.030
My nose is too small.
我的鼻子太小了。

788
00:41:13.390 --> 00:41:14.410
I mean, it works.
我是说，它还是能用的。

789
00:41:14.410 --> 00:41:15.810
I can still smell things.
我还是能闻到东西。

790
00:41:15.930 --> 00:41:18.770
I just have to be a lot closer than most people.
只是我必须比大多数人靠得更近才行。

791
00:41:19.010 --> 00:41:22.430
And then Rain, as Dwight, does this little, like, sniffy sniff.
然后雷恩饰演的德怀特做了那个小动作，就是吸鼻子的样子。

792
00:41:22.670 --> 00:41:23.750
It's really cute, actually.
其实真的很可爱。

793
00:41:23.750 --> 00:41:24.530
I thought it was cute.
我也觉得很可爱。

794
00:41:24.530 --> 00:41:27.510
We got so much mail about this, Angela.
我们收到了很多关于这部分的来信，安吉拉。

795
00:41:27.950 --> 00:41:38.750
People really wanted to know if Rain participated in this, the writing of this, or if it was a total surprise to him when he got the script.
大家真的很想知道雷恩是否参与了这部分的创作，还是说他拿到剧本时完全感到意外。

796
00:41:38.750 --> 00:41:40.790
Well, here's what Halstead said.
嗯，哈尔斯特德是这么说的。

797
00:41:41.030 --> 00:41:48.650
He said they asked Rain if there was anything about him that people made fun of or that he was ever sensitive about growing up.
他说他们问过雷恩，有没有什么关于他自己的事是别人曾取笑过，或者他成长过程中比较敏感的。

798
00:41:48.830 --> 00:41:52.090
And Rain said, okay, my nose being small.
雷恩就说，好吧，那就是我的鼻子很小。

799
00:41:52.690 --> 00:41:55.110
And it actually worked as a really funny bit.
结果这成了一个非常有趣的桥段。

800
00:41:55.290 --> 00:41:58.010
Obviously, Rain is fine with his nose now, you know.
显然，雷恩现在对自己鼻子的问题已经不在意了，你知道的。

801
00:41:58.390 --> 00:41:58.650
Yes.
是的。

802
00:41:58.810 --> 00:42:03.550
But Halstead said they liked to reach out to the actors to get things.
但霍尔斯特德说他们喜欢直接联系演员来获取信息。

803
00:42:03.550 --> 00:42:09.770
That way, it's better coming from the actor than the writer making something up that maybe, I guess, could hurt your feelings, right?
这样的话，由演员本人说出来，总比编剧瞎编一些可能会伤害到你感情的内容要好，对吧？

804
00:42:10.070 --> 00:42:10.430
Yeah.
没错。

805
00:42:10.590 --> 00:42:12.330
No, they were always really good about that.
不，他们在这方面一直做得很好。

806
00:42:12.470 --> 00:42:13.310
That's very funny.
那太搞笑了。

807
00:42:13.590 --> 00:42:15.910
As this scene goes on, other people participate.
随着这场戏的进行，其他人也参与了进来。

808
00:42:15.910 --> 00:42:22.850
And I zoomed in on the dry erase board at the end to see what Michael had written on the board under each person's name.
最后我放大了白板，想看看迈克尔在每个人的名字下面写了什么。

809
00:42:22.850 --> 00:42:37.850
The Do Not Mock list has Michael, Koi Pond and Fountain, Dwight, Nose Too Small, Aaron, Orphan, Kevin, Huge Gut, Angela, Shrimpy, Meredith, Sex with a TerroriSt.
“禁止嘲笑”名单上写着：迈克尔——锦鲤池和喷泉；德怀特——鼻子太小；亚伦——孤儿；凯文——大肚腩；安吉拉——小虾米；梅雷迪斯——和恐怖分子发生性关系。

810
00:42:38.550 --> 00:42:39.230
Shrimpy?
小虾米？

811
00:42:39.990 --> 00:42:40.670
Shrimpy?
小虾米？

812
00:42:40.810 --> 00:42:42.250
So I was like, what?
当时我就想，什么鬼？

813
00:42:42.510 --> 00:42:44.970
So I went to the script.
于是我查了剧本。

814
00:42:45.750 --> 00:42:46.890
Shrimpy is not in the script.
剧本里根本没有“小虾米”。

815
00:42:47.250 --> 00:42:50.930
It says, for Angela, Michael writes, tiny bitch.
剧本上写的是，迈克尔给安吉拉写的是“小婊子”。

816
00:42:52.050 --> 00:42:56.330
And I think Steve, in the moment, just wrote Shrimpy.
我觉得史蒂夫当时是即兴写下了“小虾米”。

817
00:42:56.950 --> 00:43:02.430
Well, there is a deleted scene for Aaron explaining why they wrote Orphan.
嗯，有一个删减片段解释了为什么他们给亚伦写了“孤儿”。

818
00:43:02.650 --> 00:43:03.170
That's right.
没错。

819
00:43:03.670 --> 00:43:06.450
Leaving the conference room, we are back with Pam and Andy.
离开会议室，我们回到帕姆和安迪这边。

820
00:43:06.590 --> 00:43:08.710
They are at their next sales call.
他们正在进行下一次销售拜访。

821
00:43:08.850 --> 00:43:13.310
They are with Kina Gifford, played by Amy Reid.
他们见的是基娜·吉福德，由艾米·里德饰演。

822
00:43:13.850 --> 00:43:16.650
Well, Angela, we know Amy Reid very well.
嗯，安吉拉，我们很了解艾米·里德。

823
00:43:16.650 --> 00:43:19.990
I thought perhaps you'd like to give us the guest star breakdown on this one.
我想你或许愿意为我们介绍一下这位客串明星。

824
00:43:19.990 --> 00:43:21.650
Oh, I would love to.
哦，我非常乐意。

825
00:43:22.030 --> 00:43:26.030
So Amy Reid, we knew her at this time as Amy Weaver.
艾米·里德，我们当时认识她时她叫艾米·韦弗。

826
00:43:26.930 --> 00:43:30.030
And she is just a dear friend of mine.
她是我的一位挚友。

827
00:43:30.130 --> 00:43:32.170
And I've known her a long time.
我认识她很久了。

828
00:43:32.390 --> 00:43:33.830
We met working at IOS.
我们是在IOS工作时认识的。

829
00:43:33.830 --> 00:43:38.310
I think our bonding moment was the song Jolene came on.
我想我们建立友谊的契机是当时响起了《乔琳》这首歌。

830
00:43:38.490 --> 00:43:39.850
And she's from Oklahoma.
她是俄克拉荷马州人。

831
00:43:39.890 --> 00:43:42.490
And my family's from Texas and Louisiana.
而我的家人来自德克萨斯州和路易斯安那州。

832
00:43:42.490 --> 00:43:52.440
And we both, without missing a beat, just started going, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene, in our southern accents.
我们俩不约而同地用南方口音唱起了“乔琳，乔琳，乔琳，乔琳”。

833
00:43:52.980 --> 00:43:54.660
I just love her so much.
我真的太喜欢她了。

834
00:43:54.740 --> 00:43:57.740
She is a hilarious actress and phenomenal writer.
她是一位搞笑的演员，也是一位了不起的编剧。

835
00:43:58.160 --> 00:44:00.840
She's still one of my dearest friends to this day.
直到今天，她依然是我最亲密的朋友之一。

836
00:44:00.840 --> 00:44:07.260
And I reached out to Amy and asked her if she could share her memories of being on the set of The Office.
我联系了艾米，问她是否愿意分享一下在《办公室》片场的回忆。

837
00:44:07.720 --> 00:44:09.440
And here's what she had to share.
以下是她分享的内容。

838
00:44:10.220 --> 00:44:16.020
First of all, she said her scenes were only with Jenna and Ed in this super small abandoned office building.
首先，她说她的戏份只和珍娜以及艾德在一个非常小的废弃办公楼里拍摄。

839
00:44:16.300 --> 00:44:20.480
There wasn't a huge cast or crew, so she really got to hang out, which is fun.
没有庞大的演职人员团队，所以她真的有很多时间可以和大家待在一起，这很有趣。

840
00:44:20.480 --> 00:44:26.380
She said one of the things she remembers is that Jenna was wearing a really huge baby bump.
她说她记得的一件事是，珍娜当时戴着一个非常大的假孕肚。

841
00:44:27.140 --> 00:44:29.700
And it was making her go to the bathroom.
这让她总想上厕所。

842
00:44:30.680 --> 00:44:35.060
And she went to the bathroom one time right before they called them back to set.
有一次在他们叫她回片场前，她去了一趟洗手间。

843
00:44:35.320 --> 00:44:42.240
And some very sweet but maybe a little too eager production assistant was knocking nonstop on the door
然后，一位非常贴心但可能有点过于积极的制片助理不停地敲门，

844
00:44:42.240 --> 00:44:45.660
while poor Jenna was trying to get the belly back on.
而可怜的珍娜当时正试图把肚子装回去。

845
00:44:45.660 --> 00:44:54.600
Then, Amy said, I only really appreciated how hot and heavy those suckers are many years later on a shoot where I had to be fake pregnant.
然后艾米说，直到多年后我在一次拍摄中需要假装怀孕，我才真正体会到那玩意儿有多沉、多热。

846
00:44:55.000 --> 00:45:00.540
She said she would like everyone to know even fake pregnant women should not be rushed in the bathroom.
她说她想让大家知道，即使是假装怀孕的女性也不应该在洗手间被催促。

847
00:45:00.760 --> 00:45:01.940
That's the lesson here.
这就是我们要学的教训。

848
00:45:03.660 --> 00:45:05.040
I knew you'd be happy.
我就知道你会高兴的。

849
00:45:05.220 --> 00:45:06.040
I know you're applauding.
我知道你在鼓掌。

850
00:45:06.280 --> 00:45:08.540
I am slow clapping that.
我正在为你缓慢鼓掌。

851
00:45:08.780 --> 00:45:10.480
Amy, thank you.
艾米，谢谢你。

852
00:45:10.700 --> 00:45:12.180
I feel so validated.
我感觉自己被深深地理解了。

853
00:45:13.520 --> 00:45:16.380
Let me explain what you have on.
让我解释一下你身上穿的这些东西。

854
00:45:16.460 --> 00:45:18.040
It's not just a belly.
那不仅仅是个假肚子。

855
00:45:18.300 --> 00:45:23.660
So I was wearing, for a reason I don't know, tights.
我当时穿了连裤袜，也不知道为什么。

856
00:45:23.860 --> 00:45:24.200
Yeah.
是啊。

857
00:45:24.680 --> 00:45:26.980
So I've got underwear, tights.
所以我穿了内衣、连裤袜。

858
00:45:27.160 --> 00:45:33.780
Then on top of that, you have on like what's like almost a wetsuit with boy shorts.
在那之上，你还穿了一件类似潜水服的东西，还有平角短裤。

859
00:45:35.340 --> 00:45:38.760
And that goes all the way up over your bra.
而且它一直包裹到你的胸罩上方。

860
00:45:39.040 --> 00:45:40.920
It's like a whole contraption.
就像一套复杂的装置。

861
00:45:40.920 --> 00:45:47.180
And then from there, they can slide in different sized bellies.
然后他们可以往里面塞入不同尺寸的假肚子。

862
00:45:47.720 --> 00:45:50.480
Then I had all my clothes on top of that.
之后我还要在外面穿上我所有的衣服。

863
00:45:50.620 --> 00:45:55.140
But I also had on a microphone and a microphone pack.
但我身上还戴着麦克风和麦克风发射器。

864
00:45:55.360 --> 00:45:57.620
With a wire taped to you.
还有用胶带粘在你身上的电线。

865
00:45:57.860 --> 00:45:58.360
Yes.
没错。

866
00:45:58.620 --> 00:46:03.440
So to go to the bathroom, I had to dismantle all of that.
所以要上厕所的话，我得把这一切全都拆下来。

867
00:46:03.640 --> 00:46:07.160
It was a good 10 minutes just to get undressed.
光是脱衣服就要花上整整十分钟。

868
00:46:07.700 --> 00:46:09.280
Then I had to pee.
然后我才能去小便。

869
00:46:09.880 --> 00:46:11.860
Then I had to put it all on.
接着我还要把这一切全都穿回去。

870
00:46:12.380 --> 00:46:12.900
Again.
重新来过。

871
00:46:13.280 --> 00:46:14.760
It was like 20 minutes.
这大概要花二十分钟。

872
00:46:15.140 --> 00:46:18.900
If I said I need to go to the bathroom, that was a 20 minute break.
如果我说我要去上厕所，那意味着二十分钟的休息时间。

873
00:46:18.900 --> 00:46:23.840
Because it was really difficult and frustrating.
因为这真的太困难、太让人沮丧了。

874
00:46:25.060 --> 00:46:27.460
And no one seemed to get it.
而且似乎没人能理解。

875
00:46:27.980 --> 00:46:30.600
And I really like I asked Alicia.
我真的问过艾丽西亚。

876
00:46:30.820 --> 00:46:37.420
I was like, Alicia, is it worth like gathering the production team together and sort of like
我说，艾丽西亚，我们有没有必要把制作团队召集起来，给他们演示一下

877
00:46:37.420 --> 00:46:39.520
taking them through all the layers?
这些层层叠叠的装备？

878
00:46:39.660 --> 00:46:44.840
Because they expect me to pee in the same amount of time that I always peed.
因为他们期望我像平时一样，在同样的时间内上完厕所。

879
00:46:44.840 --> 00:46:47.600
But I'm wearing so many more elements.
但我身上穿的东西实在太多了。

880
00:46:48.540 --> 00:46:51.700
And maybe there's like a workshop we can do.
也许我们可以办个研讨会。

881
00:46:51.900 --> 00:46:52.780
To show them.
给他们展示一下。

882
00:46:53.440 --> 00:46:53.840
Yes.
没错。

883
00:46:54.100 --> 00:46:57.920
And I actually think, Angela, correct me if I'm wrong.
我其实觉得，安吉拉，如果我说错了请纠正我。

884
00:46:58.920 --> 00:47:04.160
Wasn't there a day where Kelly Cantley, our first AD, put it on and wore it?
是不是有一天，我们的第一副导演凯莉·坎特利也穿上试了一下？

885
00:47:04.700 --> 00:47:05.100
Yes.
是的。

886
00:47:05.220 --> 00:47:08.040
Because you were like, someone else needs to experience this.
因为你当时说，得让别人也体验一下这个。

887
00:47:08.280 --> 00:47:08.800
Please.
拜托了。

888
00:47:08.980 --> 00:47:09.800
I'm begging you.
我求你们了。

889
00:47:09.800 --> 00:47:14.640
And so she put it on, you know, years later, I would have to wear the same thing.
于是她穿上了，你知道，多年以后，我也得穿上同样的东西。

890
00:47:14.640 --> 00:47:18.660
And I feel like you paved the way with our crew about what to expect.
我觉得你为我们的剧组铺平了道路，让他们知道会面临什么。

891
00:47:18.980 --> 00:47:19.720
I know.
我知道。

892
00:47:19.860 --> 00:47:20.720
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

893
00:47:20.880 --> 00:47:22.080
It was a tough road.
那是一条艰难的路。

894
00:47:22.260 --> 00:47:23.480
It was a tough paving.
铺路的过程很艰辛。

895
00:47:23.780 --> 00:47:28.000
Well, after all these years, that's the first thing Amy remembered to share with me.
好吧，这么多年过去了，这是艾米记得要跟我分享的第一件事。

896
00:47:28.320 --> 00:47:29.320
Amy, thank you.
艾米，谢谢你。

897
00:47:29.580 --> 00:47:30.280
Thank you.
谢谢你。

898
00:47:30.440 --> 00:47:31.420
I'm so touched.
我太感动了。

899
00:47:31.680 --> 00:47:35.140
She went on to say, Jenna and Ed and I were jammed into a tiny office.
她接着说，当时珍娜、埃德和我被挤在一个狭小的办公室里。

900
00:47:35.400 --> 00:47:39.480
And the director, Reggie, and the crew were outside the door on the other side.
而导演雷吉和剧组人员就在门外的另一侧。

901
00:47:39.800 --> 00:47:46.140
And at some point during downtime between takes, Jenna and I got really chatty with each other.
在拍摄间隙的休息时间里，我和珍娜聊得非常投机。

902
00:47:46.240 --> 00:47:51.200
And I guess we were kind of leaving Ed out of the conversation with very little room to jump in.
我想我们当时可能有点冷落了埃德，让他几乎插不上话。

903
00:47:51.240 --> 00:47:55.500
And he finally just interrupted and said, do you two know each other?
最后他终于忍不住打断我们说，你们俩认识吗？

904
00:47:57.720 --> 00:48:02.200
Because you had met Amy through me and we had become all a group of friends.
因为你通过我认识了艾米，我们后来就都成了朋友。

905
00:48:02.600 --> 00:48:02.820
Yeah.
是啊。

906
00:48:03.200 --> 00:48:03.560
Yeah.
没错。

907
00:48:03.560 --> 00:48:07.080
The last thing Amy shared was this.
艾米分享的最后一件事是这样的。

908
00:48:07.680 --> 00:48:13.620
One random thing that made a huge impression on me that day was when Jenna invited me to her trailer for lunch.
那天有一件小事给我留下了非常深刻的印象，就是珍娜邀请我去她的拖车里吃午饭。

909
00:48:13.780 --> 00:48:18.920
As we sat there chatting, it somehow came up about the beginning of you and her's friendship.
我们坐在那儿聊天时，不知怎么就聊到了你和她友谊的开端。

910
00:48:19.680 --> 00:48:24.120
Jenna shared about the transition you guys had by being on the cast of The Office,
珍娜分享了你们在出演《办公室》期间所经历的转变，

911
00:48:24.120 --> 00:48:31.180
how you two really bonded over going from inconsistent acting careers to suddenly being in the limelight.
聊到你们是如何从不稳定的演艺生涯，突然之间变得备受瞩目，并因此建立了深厚的感情。

912
00:48:31.320 --> 00:48:35.360
And the impact and weight of being on The Office and the adjustment to that.
还有出演《办公室》所带来的影响和压力，以及对那种生活的适应过程。

913
00:48:35.480 --> 00:48:38.720
And how you two were together through all of it.
以及你们是如何一起度过这一切的。

914
00:48:38.880 --> 00:48:44.480
Through that transition, you balanced earnest humility and the thrill of being on the number one comedy.
在那种转变中，你们既保持了真诚的谦逊，又享受着身处全美第一喜剧的兴奋感。

915
00:48:45.320 --> 00:48:45.900
Wow.
哇。

916
00:48:46.140 --> 00:48:47.240
Now I'm like crying.
我现在都要哭了。

917
00:48:48.860 --> 00:48:50.520
I thought that was wonderful.
我觉得那太美好了。

918
00:48:50.520 --> 00:48:51.260
Now I'm like really moved.
我现在真的很感动。

919
00:48:51.520 --> 00:48:52.160
I know.
我知道。

920
00:48:52.820 --> 00:48:53.220
Yeah.
是啊。

921
00:48:53.220 --> 00:48:55.580
I mean, that was true.
我是说，那是真的。

922
00:48:55.580 --> 00:49:00.400
I can't imagine having to have done that without you, Angela.
安吉拉，我无法想象如果没有你，我该怎么熬过来。

923
00:49:01.020 --> 00:49:01.980
Aw, lady.
噢，亲爱的。

924
00:49:02.480 --> 00:49:03.760
It was overwhelming.
那真的让人难以招架。

925
00:49:03.760 --> 00:49:07.820
It was all of your professional dreams coming true,
那是你所有职业梦想成真的时刻，

926
00:49:07.820 --> 00:49:13.420
but all the ways that you don't think that that is going to impact your life in weird ways.
但你根本想不到它会以各种奇怪的方式影响你的生活。

927
00:49:13.420 --> 00:49:20.320
You know, your face on television every week and what that does,
你知道，每周你的脸都会出现在电视上，那种感觉，

928
00:49:20.480 --> 00:49:23.520
how it changes different relationships or friendships,
它会如何改变不同的人际关系或友谊，

929
00:49:24.080 --> 00:49:28.820
how your time is not your own when you are on a television show,
当你出演一部电视剧时，你的时间就不再属于你自己了，

930
00:49:28.980 --> 00:49:36.000
the long hours, but then all of the additional promotional work that takes up your weekends
漫长的工作时间，还有所有那些占用你周末的额外宣传工作，

931
00:49:36.000 --> 00:49:40.480
and how you can't go to things anymore.
以及你再也无法参加各种活动了。

932
00:49:40.480 --> 00:49:44.540
And to have someone to go through that with and navigate that with.
能有一个人陪你一起经历这些，一起应对这些，真的很重要。

933
00:49:44.620 --> 00:49:45.760
And you're so excited.
而且你当时会感到非常兴奋。

934
00:49:46.200 --> 00:49:51.080
But then the Midwesterner in me would always feel like very shy about it.
但作为中西部人，我内心总会对此感到非常害羞。

935
00:49:51.120 --> 00:49:52.780
And I think we had that in common.
我想我们在这点上很有共鸣。

936
00:49:54.040 --> 00:49:55.840
I mean, she really nailed it.
我是说，她真的说得太准了。

937
00:49:56.380 --> 00:49:56.740
I know.
我知道。

938
00:49:56.880 --> 00:49:59.660
I thought, what great observations from her day on set.
我在想，她在那天片场观察得真仔细。

939
00:50:00.340 --> 00:50:00.780
Yeah.
是啊。

940
00:50:01.180 --> 00:50:03.140
Well, you know I feel the same way, lady.
嗯，你知道我也一样，亲爱的。

941
00:50:03.340 --> 00:50:03.760
My gosh.
天哪。

942
00:50:03.880 --> 00:50:09.660
How would I have gotten through, you know, the last 18 years, oh my word, without your friendship?
如果没有你的友谊，我该怎么度过这，天哪，过去的18年啊？

943
00:50:09.660 --> 00:50:11.080
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

944
00:50:11.280 --> 00:50:11.780
18.
18年了。

945
00:50:12.520 --> 00:50:15.480
I have one last fun tidbit about this scene.
关于这一幕，我还有一个最后的小趣事。

946
00:50:16.180 --> 00:50:20.060
Warren reminded me of it, and I went and looked for it immediately.
沃伦提醒了我，我立刻就去查证了一下。

947
00:50:20.760 --> 00:50:25.500
There is a photo of our daughter, Isabel, in a frame just over Amy's shoulder.
在艾米的肩膀上方，有一个相框，里面是我们女儿伊莎贝尔的照片。

948
00:50:25.760 --> 00:50:31.000
If you go to 11 minutes, 35 seconds, you can see Isabel in the little silver frame.
如果你把进度条拉到11分35秒，就能看到那个银色小相框里的伊莎贝尔。

949
00:50:31.180 --> 00:50:32.440
She's smiling so big.
她笑得特别灿烂。

950
00:50:32.440 --> 00:50:33.720
She's in her car seat.
她当时正坐在婴儿安全座椅里。

951
00:50:33.720 --> 00:50:36.500
I love that Phil Shea did that for us.
我真喜欢菲尔·谢伊为我们做的那件事。

952
00:50:36.780 --> 00:50:40.180
It just, oh my gosh, warmed my heart so much.
天哪，那真的太暖心了。

953
00:50:40.340 --> 00:50:41.420
I saw it too.
我也看到了。

954
00:50:41.980 --> 00:50:44.280
Oh, oh, and one last thing.
哦，对了，还有最后一件事。

955
00:50:44.420 --> 00:50:46.180
I know I've had a lot to say about this scene.
我知道关于这场戏我已经说了很多了。

956
00:50:46.720 --> 00:50:52.740
So Miss Gifford and Andy bond over this birthing teacher named Miss Janet.
吉福德小姐和安迪因为一位叫珍妮特小姐的分娩老师而建立了感情。

957
00:50:53.220 --> 00:50:55.200
Well, Janet is my sister's name.
嗯，我姐姐也叫珍妮特。

958
00:50:56.080 --> 00:50:56.560
Hmm.
嗯。

959
00:50:57.620 --> 00:50:58.800
That's so sweet.
太贴心了。

960
00:50:59.060 --> 00:50:59.860
So there you go.
就是这样。

961
00:50:59.860 --> 00:51:02.280
That's everything that I had for that scene.
关于这场戏我要说的就是这些。

962
00:51:02.600 --> 00:51:04.360
Well, I think we should take a break.
好吧，我觉得我们该休息一下了。

963
00:51:04.400 --> 00:51:08.640
And when we come back, we're going to talk about how you eat like a squirrel, Angela.
等回来之后，我们要聊聊你像松鼠一样吃东西的事，安吉拉。

964
00:51:09.140 --> 00:51:10.140
Okay, great.
好的，太棒了。

965
00:51:19.100 --> 00:51:22.400
We are back, and we are still in the conference room.
我们回来了，现在还在会议室里。

966
00:51:22.960 --> 00:51:26.800
People are still talking about the things that bother them.
大家还在讨论那些让他们心烦的事。

967
00:51:26.940 --> 00:51:30.300
And Angela, you do not like it when people say you eat like a squirrel.
安吉拉，你不喜欢别人说你吃东西像松鼠。

968
00:51:30.740 --> 00:51:31.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

969
00:51:31.760 --> 00:51:33.200
You don't care for that.
你不喜欢那样。

970
00:51:33.400 --> 00:51:34.440
I don't care for that.
我不喜欢那样。

971
00:51:34.440 --> 00:51:38.580
And also, I'm afraid someone's going to throw me around like a football because I'm so petite.
而且，我还担心有人会像扔橄榄球一样把我扔来扔去，因为我太娇小了。

972
00:51:39.140 --> 00:51:39.480
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

973
00:51:40.640 --> 00:51:49.700
Aaron is going to interrupt this meeting and let Michael know that someone has called to inform them that one of the coy died.
亚伦会打断会议，告诉迈克尔有人打电话来说锦鲤死了一条。

974
00:51:50.300 --> 00:51:52.040
And they want him to pay for it.
他们要他赔钱。

975
00:51:52.100 --> 00:51:53.320
It's going to be $300.
要300美元。

976
00:51:54.220 --> 00:51:56.200
Aren't coy, like, crazy expensive?
锦鲤不是很贵吗？

977
00:51:56.200 --> 00:51:58.200
Yeah, they are.
是啊，很贵。

978
00:51:58.560 --> 00:52:11.520
And Halstead shared that they had pitched around in the writer's room a kind of extension of this storyline because they found out that some coy can, like, cost as much as $2,000.
哈尔斯特德分享说，他们在编剧室里讨论过这个故事线的延伸，因为他们发现有些锦鲤的价格高达2000美元。

979
00:52:11.520 --> 00:52:21.540
So, at one point, the coy that Michael killed was going to be worth $2,000, and that Michael was going to pay for it.
所以，一度曾设想迈克尔杀掉的那条锦鲤价值2000美元，而且迈克尔会赔钱。

980
00:52:21.680 --> 00:52:26.380
He was going to get it because he was going to want to see a $2,000 fish.
他会把它拿回来，因为他想看看价值2000美元的鱼长什么样。

981
00:52:26.640 --> 00:52:33.740
And then back at the office, he was going to cook it in the toaster oven and eat it.
然后回到办公室，他会用烤箱把它烤了吃掉。

982
00:52:33.860 --> 00:52:34.260
No!
不！

983
00:52:36.140 --> 00:52:42.460
Yes, this was the pitch, but that ultimately Michael was going to chicken out and he was just going to throw it away.
是的，这就是当时的构思，但最终迈克尔会临阵退缩，直接把它扔掉。

984
00:52:43.260 --> 00:52:48.380
And Halstead said, by the time they got to the end of this pitch, they were like, you know what?
哈尔斯特德说，当他们讲完这个构思时，他们觉得，你知道吗？

985
00:52:48.460 --> 00:52:49.320
It's disturbing.
这太让人不安了。

986
00:52:49.560 --> 00:52:55.140
We're going to, how about the coy is just $300 and there's no eating of the coy.
我们还是把锦鲤的价格定为300美元吧，而且也不要吃锦鲤了。

987
00:52:55.440 --> 00:52:57.180
Or throwing it away.
或者扔掉它。

988
00:52:57.560 --> 00:53:01.200
Yes, and Halstead said, I'm very happy we changed that.
是的，哈尔斯特德说，我很高兴我们改了主意。

989
00:53:01.680 --> 00:53:04.100
Well, you know, Michael wouldn't have thrown it away.
嗯，你知道，迈克尔才不会把它扔掉呢。

990
00:53:04.120 --> 00:53:07.280
If he didn't eat it, he would have had a proper burial for it.
如果他不吃的话，他会给它举行一场体面的葬礼。

991
00:53:07.500 --> 00:53:09.560
That's most likely, yes.
很有可能，是的。

992
00:53:09.820 --> 00:53:11.420
And there would have been a coy funeral.
而且还会有一场锦鲤葬礼。

993
00:53:11.660 --> 00:53:14.600
Yes, and then maybe Creed would have digged it up and eaten it.
是的，然后克里德可能会把它挖出来吃掉。

994
00:53:14.720 --> 00:53:15.660
Oh, gross.
哦，恶心。

995
00:53:17.080 --> 00:53:20.420
I did love when Creed was like, oh, man, you're paying way too much for worMs.
我真的很喜欢克里德说的那句：天哪，你买虫子花太多钱了。

996
00:53:20.420 --> 00:53:21.320
Who's your worm guy?
你的虫子供应商是谁？

997
00:53:22.080 --> 00:53:23.280
Who's your worm guy?
你的虫子供应商是谁？

998
00:53:23.980 --> 00:53:24.760
So funny.
太搞笑了。

999
00:53:24.940 --> 00:53:25.960
Put that on a shirt.
把它印在衬衫上吧。

1000
00:53:29.440 --> 00:53:33.740
Jim is going to get Michael aside and say, I have a strategy.
吉姆会把迈克尔拉到一边说，我有个策略。

1001
00:53:34.340 --> 00:53:40.120
I think maybe you should make fun of yourself for falling into the coy pond.
我觉得也许你应该拿自己掉进锦鲤池的事开开玩笑。

1002
00:53:40.660 --> 00:53:43.260
Yeah, and that will diffuse everyone else, right?
对，这样就能化解其他人的尴尬，对吧？

1003
00:53:43.720 --> 00:53:44.140
Yeah.
没错。

1004
00:53:44.380 --> 00:53:46.620
They won't be able to tell jokes because you've covered it.
因为你已经自嘲过了，他们就没法再拿这事开玩笑了。

1005
00:53:47.100 --> 00:53:48.760
So Michael's going to try it.
所以迈克尔打算试一试。

1006
00:53:48.960 --> 00:53:50.660
He's like, all right, I'll try it.
他当时想，好吧，我试试。

1007
00:53:50.780 --> 00:53:53.920
And at first, it goes well.
起初，效果还不错。

1008
00:53:54.740 --> 00:53:55.780
And then it doesn't.
但后来就不行了。

1009
00:53:55.780 --> 00:53:57.560
But he goes too far.
他做得太过火了。

1010
00:53:57.660 --> 00:53:59.240
He goes too far.
他做得太过火了。

1011
00:53:59.240 --> 00:54:01.200
And he knows he's going too far.
而且他自己也知道做得太过火了。

1012
00:54:01.400 --> 00:54:03.660
This was such a brilliant performance.
这表演真是太精彩了。

1013
00:54:04.020 --> 00:54:11.220
It's like that thing when you're like talking to someone and you know that moment you went past where you should have stopped.
就像你和别人聊天时，明明知道自己已经说过了头，本该停下的那一刻。

1014
00:54:11.440 --> 00:54:13.740
And in your own brain, you're like, stop, stop.
你在心里对自己说，停下，快停下。

1015
00:54:13.900 --> 00:54:14.660
But you can't.
但你就是停不下来。

1016
00:54:15.040 --> 00:54:15.420
Yes.
没错。

1017
00:54:15.560 --> 00:54:16.880
And he just keeps talking.
而他还在不停地说。

1018
00:54:17.200 --> 00:54:22.060
He keeps saying embarrassing things about his life that aren't even about the coy pond.
他一直在说些关于自己生活的尴尬事，甚至都跟锦鲤池没关系了。

1019
00:54:22.540 --> 00:54:26.640
Well, Warren shared with us that this was one of his favorite comedy bits.
沃伦跟我们分享过，这是他最喜欢的喜剧桥段之一。

1020
00:54:27.320 --> 00:54:31.960
And he said when Michael goes too far with it, they had even more pitch, Jenna.
他说当迈克尔做得太过火时，他们其实还有更多梗，珍娜。

1021
00:54:32.140 --> 00:54:34.300
They had even more jokes in the pipeline here.
他们准备了更多的笑话。

1022
00:54:34.640 --> 00:54:36.840
He said he and Halstead loved writing this runner.
他说他和霍尔斯特德很喜欢写这个连贯的笑点。

1023
00:54:37.100 --> 00:54:39.200
Here were some that didn't make it in the show.
以下是一些没能放进正片里的内容。

1024
00:54:39.360 --> 00:54:39.840
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

1025
00:54:40.120 --> 00:54:40.780
I'm ready.
准备好了。

1026
00:54:41.300 --> 00:54:46.120
I can't listen to talk radio when I drive because I get scared that someone else is in the car.
我开车时不能听谈话广播，因为我总害怕车里还有别人。

1027
00:54:46.920 --> 00:54:47.400
Okay.
好吧。

1028
00:54:47.900 --> 00:54:52.280
Then there was another one where Michael locks himself in a dog cage at Kmart.
还有一个桥段是迈克尔把自己锁在凯马特的狗笼子里。

1029
00:54:52.600 --> 00:54:53.940
No one could get him out.
没人能把他弄出来。

1030
00:54:54.100 --> 00:54:54.760
He was stuck.
他被困住了。

1031
00:54:54.880 --> 00:54:56.420
And they had to call the fire department.
他们不得不叫消防队来。

1032
00:54:57.240 --> 00:54:57.440
Okay.
好吧。

1033
00:54:58.500 --> 00:55:06.340
Then there was a take when Michael goes so far and cuts so deep at himself that he makes himself cry.
还有一个版本是迈克尔做得太过火，把自己损得太狠，结果把自己给说哭了。

1034
00:55:07.120 --> 00:55:10.920
And Warren said Steve's performance was so phenomenal.
沃伦说史蒂夫的表演简直太惊人了。

1035
00:55:11.020 --> 00:55:12.920
It was his favorite take.
那是他最喜欢的一个版本。

1036
00:55:13.120 --> 00:55:14.340
He fought really hard.
他极力争取保留。

1037
00:55:14.520 --> 00:55:16.420
But too many people disagreed.
但反对的人太多了。

1038
00:55:16.520 --> 00:55:17.560
They said it was too depressing.
他们说那太压抑了。

1039
00:55:17.560 --> 00:55:19.240
And Warren lost the battle.
最后沃伦输了。

1040
00:55:19.260 --> 00:55:20.800
So it ends with the,
所以最后呈现的是……

1041
00:55:21.640 --> 00:55:22.280
Wow.
哇。

1042
00:55:24.200 --> 00:55:28.540
This was definitely one of those scenes where we would go to the candy bag.
这绝对是那种我们会去“糖果袋”里翻找素材的场景。

1043
00:55:28.720 --> 00:55:31.180
They would always have extra stuff for scenes like this.
像这样的场景，他们总是会准备额外的素材。

1044
00:55:31.760 --> 00:55:38.540
And I know we say this a lot, you guys, but Steve is so amazing because he could dial it up
我知道我们经常这么说，但史蒂夫真的很了不起，因为他能收放自如，

1045
00:55:38.540 --> 00:55:42.320
or dial it down or cry or just, he could do anything.
无论是加强还是减弱，或是哭泣，他什么都能演。

1046
00:55:42.360 --> 00:55:43.800
He was so impressive.
他太让人印象深刻了。

1047
00:55:44.240 --> 00:55:45.440
I would lose myself.
我经常会看入迷。

1048
00:55:45.560 --> 00:55:46.320
I've said this before.
我以前说过。

1049
00:55:46.460 --> 00:55:49.380
I'd be like, oh crap, I'm supposed to be reacting as Angela Martin.
我当时会想，糟了，我应该以安吉拉·马丁的身份做出反应才对。

1050
00:55:49.380 --> 00:55:52.780
And instead I was just there like, oh my gosh, Steve is crushing it.
结果我只是站在那儿想，天哪，史蒂夫演得太棒了。

1051
00:55:53.120 --> 00:55:54.520
I wish I could have been there.
真希望我当时也在场。

1052
00:55:55.000 --> 00:55:56.960
I would have loved to have watched this.
我真希望能看看这一幕。

1053
00:55:57.100 --> 00:56:02.400
That was maybe one of the things that was so fun about re-watching this episode was that
重温这一集最有趣的地方或许就在于，

1054
00:56:02.400 --> 00:56:06.660
I was really watching this as a fan because I wasn't there.
我是真的以粉丝的视角在看，因为我当时不在现场。

1055
00:56:06.780 --> 00:56:10.720
So I don't have memories of what else went on or what got cut.
所以我对当时还发生了什么，或者剪掉了什么完全没有记忆。

1056
00:56:11.000 --> 00:56:12.500
I'm just watching it.
我只是在看剧而已。

1057
00:56:12.620 --> 00:56:13.200
It's great.
这感觉太棒了。

1058
00:56:13.760 --> 00:56:16.740
I think that's why I got so tickled when Andy says,
我想这就是为什么当安迪说出那句台词时，我会觉得那么好笑，

1059
00:56:16.740 --> 00:56:20.820
it looks like someone's got a case of the definitely's because I wasn't there when you
“看来有人得了‘确定症’”，因为你们拍那场戏的时候，

1060
00:56:20.820 --> 00:56:21.660
guys did that.
我并不在场。

1061
00:56:22.080 --> 00:56:22.280
Yeah.
没错。

1062
00:56:22.960 --> 00:56:28.440
Well, now, Angela, I've got a fan question for you because you are in the break room
好了，安吉拉，现在有个粉丝问题要问你，因为你在休息室里，

1063
00:56:28.440 --> 00:56:30.280
and you are eating a nut.
而且你在吃坚果。

1064
00:56:31.860 --> 00:56:32.700
Heather C.
来自英国利兹的希瑟·C（Heather C.）问，

1065
00:56:32.960 --> 00:56:34.840
from Leeds in the UK said,
“安吉拉，我最喜欢的安吉拉时刻之一，就是你在休息室里像松鼠一样吃东西的那段。

1066
00:56:35.000 --> 00:56:40.860
Angela, one of my favorite Angela moments ever is the bit where you eat like a squirrel
还有你把包装纸重新包好的那部分，真的让我笑得不行。

1067
00:56:40.860 --> 00:56:41.920
in the break room.
你究竟是怎么想出这个桥段的？

1068
00:56:41.920 --> 00:56:46.860
Also, the part where you wrap your packaging back up cracks me up so much.
你是不是看了很多松鼠吃东西的视频？"

1069
00:56:47.020 --> 00:56:49.360
How did you come up with this bit exactly?
希瑟，这太搞笑了。

1070
00:56:49.860 --> 00:56:53.540
Did you perhaps watch a lot of videos of squirrels eating?
谢谢你欣赏我那段松鼠吃东西的表演。

1071
00:56:54.720 --> 00:56:56.160
Heather, that's hilarious.
说实话，我没看过任何视频。

1072
00:56:56.580 --> 00:57:01.060
Well, thank you for appreciating my squirrel eating performance.
我只是，你知道，我见过松鼠吃东西，我运用了我个人的生活观察。

1073
00:57:01.660 --> 00:57:04.720
You know, honestly, I didn't watch any videos.
而且你要知道，剧本里关于那场戏的舞台指示是：

1074
00:57:04.720 --> 00:57:11.620
I just, you know, I've seen a squirrel eat and I use my own personal life observation.
“梅雷迪斯、凯文、安吉拉和奥斯卡坐在桌边。

1075
00:57:12.220 --> 00:57:16.760
And just so you know, the stage direction in the script for the scene was,
安吉拉啃着一颗杏仁，像松鼠一样用双手捧着。”

1076
00:57:17.220 --> 00:57:20.040
Meredith, Kevin, Angela, and Oscar sit at tables.
所以我知道我必须用双手捧着，就像我做的那样。

1077
00:57:20.760 --> 00:57:25.060
Angela gnaws at an almond, holding it with two hands like a squirrel.
然后我就按照我以为松鼠会吃东西的方式把它吃了。

1078
00:57:25.660 --> 00:57:29.260
So I knew I had to hold it with two hands, just the way I'm doing it.
剧本里接着写道，她把剩下的杏仁放回保鲜膜里。

1079
00:57:29.640 --> 00:57:32.640
And then I just ate it the way I thought a squirrel would eat it.
所以那是剧本里写好的。

1080
00:57:33.120 --> 00:57:38.860
And then in the script, it goes on to say, she puts the rest of her almond back into saran wrap.
但我折叠和处理的方式，你知道，那纯粹是我当时即兴发挥的。

1081
00:57:39.600 --> 00:57:40.960
So that was in the script.
我拍那场戏拍得特别开心。

1082
00:57:40.960 --> 00:57:44.800
But how I folded it and did it, you know, it was just me sort of playing in the moment.
我们一直在笑。

1083
00:57:45.320 --> 00:57:47.180
I had so much fun doing that.
就像布莱恩和奥斯卡，我们大家都笑个不停。

1084
00:57:47.180 --> 00:57:48.380
And we kept laughing.
作为你的死党，我要郑重声明，你平时吃东西根本不是那样。

1085
00:57:48.780 --> 00:57:52.100
Like Brian and Oscar, we all kept cracking up.
我们都知道你吃手撕奶酪时是直接咬的。

1086
00:57:52.400 --> 00:57:57.840
Well, as your BFF, I will go on record to say that you do not actually eat like that.
哦，没错。

1087
00:57:58.320 --> 00:58:00.960
We all know you bite right into the string cheese.
我不会用双手捧着它啃。

1088
00:58:00.960 --> 00:58:01.720
Oh, yeah.
我会直接大口咬下去。

1089
00:58:01.940 --> 00:58:04.040
I'm not holding it with two hands, gnawing at it.
你根本不会把它撕成丝什么的。

1090
00:58:04.100 --> 00:58:05.060
I'm going to chomp at it.
你就是直接吃掉。

1091
00:58:05.120 --> 00:58:07.140
You're not stringing it or anything.
但你确实经常把没吃完的东西包起来。

1092
00:58:07.460 --> 00:58:08.840
You're just eating it.
这是真的。

1093
00:58:09.080 --> 00:58:13.080
But you do often wrap up the second half of whatever you haven't eaten.
确实如此。

1094
00:58:13.240 --> 00:58:13.960
This is true.
没错。

1095
00:58:14.060 --> 00:58:14.320
That is true.
如果你现在打开我的冰箱，里面可能有四颗葡萄，用一小块锡纸包着。

1096
00:58:14.480 --> 00:58:15.160
This is true.
你打算晚点吃掉它们。

1097
00:58:15.400 --> 00:58:20.620
If you open my fridge right now, there's like four grapes wrapped up in a little piece of tinfoil.
我会的。

1098
00:58:20.820 --> 00:58:22.040
You're going to eat those later.
听着，回到帕姆和安迪的会议上，安迪确实有点失控了。

1099
00:58:22.280 --> 00:58:22.880
I will.
我当时不在场。

1100
00:58:22.880 --> 00:58:32.800
So listen, back in the meeting with Pam and Andy, Andy is really gets a little out of control.
你们拍那场戏的时候。

1101
00:58:33.020 --> 00:58:37.080
He's like smothering Pam's belly with his face.
他简直是用脸在蹭帕姆的肚子。

1102
00:58:37.340 --> 00:58:40.020
Well, they've just finally decided to lean into it.
嗯，他们终于决定顺其自然了。

1103
00:58:40.200 --> 00:58:40.900
Yeah, fine.
行吧，没问题。

1104
00:58:40.900 --> 00:58:41.600
We're a couple.
我们是一对。

1105
00:58:41.800 --> 00:58:44.260
This is our baby to try to make the sale.
这是我们为了促成交易而假扮的宝宝。

1106
00:58:44.500 --> 00:58:47.120
But we learn a lot about Andy in this moment.
但我们在这瞬间了解到了安迪的很多事。

1107
00:58:47.580 --> 00:58:48.180
We do.
确实。

1108
00:58:48.500 --> 00:58:55.520
And afterwards, Pam says, you know, that was great, but maybe you took it a little far.
事后帕姆说，你知道，那很棒，但你可能有点过火了。

1109
00:58:55.760 --> 00:58:57.780
And he's like, yeah, yeah, it was.
他说，是啊，确实是。

1110
00:58:57.900 --> 00:59:00.240
Maybe the belly kissing was a little much.
亲肚子可能有点过了。

1111
00:59:00.700 --> 00:59:03.020
And he reveals a couple of things.
然后他透露了几件事。

1112
00:59:03.420 --> 00:59:12.840
One, he reveals that it was nice for him to pretend for a minute that he was part of a couple with a baby on the way.
第一，他透露说，能假装一会儿自己是有宝宝的伴侣，对他来说感觉很好。

1113
00:59:13.060 --> 00:59:14.440
Oh, that broke my heart.
噢，那真让我心碎。

1114
00:59:14.680 --> 00:59:15.320
I know.
我知道。

1115
00:59:15.320 --> 00:59:21.440
Oh, and then he also reveals that maybe he has a little crush on Aaron.
噢，他还透露说，他可能对亚伦有点好感。

1116
00:59:22.120 --> 00:59:22.600
Hmm.
嗯。

1117
00:59:23.200 --> 00:59:23.560
Hmm.
嗯。

1118
00:59:24.120 --> 00:59:24.780
Well, guess what?
好吧，你猜怎么着？

1119
00:59:24.920 --> 00:59:30.480
Meredith's roommate is friends with the night janitor at the office building where Michael fell.
梅雷迪思的室友和迈克尔摔倒那栋办公楼的夜班清洁工是朋友。

1120
00:59:30.480 --> 00:59:32.940
And she's got a copy of the security footage.
她有监控录像的副本。

1121
00:59:33.220 --> 00:59:34.360
Yes, she does.
没错，她有。

1122
00:59:34.760 --> 00:59:42.600
Everyone is going to gather around Meredith's computer and we are going to see Michael fall into the koi ponds.
大家都要围在梅雷迪思的电脑前，我们要看迈克尔掉进锦鲤池的画面了。

1123
00:59:43.200 --> 00:59:51.360
We got so many fan questions about the fall into the koi pond, and we're going to do our best to break it down for you.
我们收到了很多粉丝关于掉进锦鲤池的问题，我们会尽力为大家详细拆解。

1124
00:59:51.360 --> 01:00:01.360
Starting with Callie B from Rogers, Arkansas, who asked, where was the security footage of Steve falling into the pond filmed?
首先是来自阿肯色州罗杰斯市的凯莉·B，她问，史蒂夫掉进池塘的监控录像是在哪里拍的？

1125
01:00:02.200 --> 01:00:06.500
Randy told us that we shot the koi pond just down the street from our studios.
兰迪告诉我们，锦鲤池是在离我们工作室不远的一条街上拍的。

1126
01:00:06.920 --> 01:00:11.900
They were a neon sign manufacturing business called Knights of Neon.
那是一家叫“霓虹骑士”的霓虹灯制造公司。

1127
01:00:12.300 --> 01:00:18.500
This business has operated for over 30 years, and they make custom neon signs for commercial use.
这家公司经营了30多年，专门制作商业用的定制霓虹灯。

1128
01:00:18.500 --> 01:00:25.140
I really hope their logo is like a knight in, like, metal armor holding up like a shield.
我真希望他们的标志是一个穿着金属盔甲、举着盾牌的骑士。

1129
01:00:25.380 --> 01:00:26.620
Knights of Neon.
霓虹骑士。

1130
01:00:27.020 --> 01:00:31.220
Oh, well, it's spelled N-I-G-H-T-S of Neon.
噢，那个词拼写是N-I-G-H-T-S（夜晚）的霓虹。

1131
01:00:31.260 --> 01:00:31.940
Oh, boo.
噢，真扫兴。

1132
01:00:32.720 --> 01:00:33.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1133
01:00:33.540 --> 01:00:34.040
I'm kidding.
我开玩笑的。

1134
01:00:34.220 --> 01:00:34.600
I'm kidding.
我开玩笑的。

1135
01:00:35.840 --> 01:00:42.880
This company, Knights of Neon, had a really big empty warehouse, and that's why we picked it.
这家“霓虹骑士”公司有一个非常大的空仓库，所以我们选了那里。

1136
01:00:42.880 --> 01:00:52.780
We rented it out for a whole week, and Michael Gallenberg and his construction coordinator, Tim James, they started by laying down, like,
我们把它租下来整整一周，迈克尔·加伦伯格和他的施工协调员蒂姆·詹姆斯，他们先是铺设了，就像是，

1137
01:00:52.840 --> 01:00:56.620
a waterproof liner over the entire floor of the warehouse.
在仓库整个地板上铺了一层防水衬垫。

1138
01:00:57.220 --> 01:01:08.500
Then they built a koi pond on top of it that held 1,000 gallons of filtered water, and then they made the walkways on top of it.
然后他们在上面建了一个能容纳1000加仑过滤水的锦鲤池，接着在上面做了人行道。

1139
01:01:08.500 --> 01:01:12.180
But they also then set up two cameras.
但他们随后还架设了两台摄像机。

1140
01:01:12.900 --> 01:01:21.460
Reggie really wanted, like, this motorized surveillance camera that would sort of sweep the lobby back and forth.
雷吉真的很想要那种能在大厅里来回扫视的电动监控摄像头。

1141
01:01:21.760 --> 01:01:29.500
And so Matt Soane created this effect by using a tripod with a fluid head mounted on top of a tall ladder.
所以马特·索恩通过把一个带有液压云台的三脚架安装在高梯子上，制造出了这种效果。

1142
01:01:29.500 --> 01:01:33.460
So they made this fakie, sweepie security camera.
所以他们做了一个假装在扫视的监控摄像头。

1143
01:01:33.460 --> 01:01:39.180
I guess this sweeping shot is best seen in the deleted scenes around four minutes, nine seconds.
我想这个扫视镜头在删除片段里四分零九秒左右看得最清楚。

1144
01:01:39.540 --> 01:01:40.120
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1145
01:01:40.320 --> 01:01:42.000
Go to the deleted scenes for this episode.
去看这一集的删除片段吧。

1146
01:01:42.000 --> 01:01:43.240
It's the last one.
那是最后一个。

1147
01:01:43.280 --> 01:01:47.840
It's the whole entire footage of Michael falling in.
那是迈克尔掉进去的完整录像。

1148
01:01:48.180 --> 01:01:51.340
And when I watched it, I was like, oh, wow.
当我看完的时候，我心想，哇。

1149
01:01:51.520 --> 01:01:55.100
I didn't realize how long Steve was in the water.
我没意识到史蒂夫在水里待了那么久。

1150
01:01:55.380 --> 01:01:57.600
I mean, they really went for it.
我是说，他们真的是拼了。

1151
01:01:58.660 --> 01:02:07.360
Well, I guess we added another stationary, non-moving B camera that was angled a little bit more at the front.
嗯，我想我们又加了一台固定的、不动的B机位，角度稍微更朝向正面一点。

1152
01:02:07.900 --> 01:02:11.320
Derek Carver was our B camera operator that day.
那天我们的B机位摄影师是德里克·卡弗。

1153
01:02:11.480 --> 01:02:19.640
And the footage that you end up seeing on this tape that everyone's watching is that B camera footage, the still footage.
而你们在这盘录像带上看到的、大家都在看的画面，就是那台B机位拍的，也就是静止的画面。

1154
01:02:20.120 --> 01:02:20.820
All right.
好的。

1155
01:02:21.120 --> 01:02:22.240
Next question.
下一个问题。

1156
01:02:22.520 --> 01:02:24.540
This one comes from Braylon M.
这个问题来自布雷伦·M。

1157
01:02:24.740 --> 01:02:26.000
in Seattle, Washington.
他住在华盛顿州西雅图。

1158
01:02:26.000 --> 01:02:30.760
Were there actually koi in the pond that Michael falls in?
迈克尔掉进去的那个池塘里真的有锦鲤吗？

1159
01:02:31.400 --> 01:02:32.160
Yes.
有的。

1160
01:02:32.920 --> 01:02:33.560
Yes.
是的。

1161
01:02:33.860 --> 01:02:42.060
Randy told us that we went with our usual animal training company, which was Bob Dunn's Animal Rentals in Sylmar, California.
兰迪告诉我们，我们找的是惯常合作的动物训练公司，也就是位于加州希尔马的鲍勃·邓恩动物租赁公司。

1162
01:02:42.500 --> 01:02:44.420
They do it all, clearly.
他们什么都干，显而易见。

1163
01:02:44.800 --> 01:02:45.740
They do.
确实。

1164
01:02:46.140 --> 01:02:54.040
The head trainer there is Denise Sanders, but we had to also employ a special koi wrangler named Mike Long.
那里的首席训练师是丹妮丝·桑德斯，但我们还必须雇佣一位专门的锦鲤管理员，名叫迈克·朗。

1165
01:02:54.040 --> 01:02:56.340
What was Kelly Cantley thinking?
凯莉·坎特利当时在想什么呢？

1166
01:02:56.720 --> 01:02:59.120
She's had a fruit fly wrangler.
她雇过果蝇管理员。

1167
01:02:59.300 --> 01:03:01.220
She's had a koi wrangler.
她雇过锦鲤管理员。

1168
01:03:01.720 --> 01:03:03.420
Several cat wranglers.
还有好几位猫咪管理员。

1169
01:03:04.100 --> 01:03:04.800
Fascinating.
太迷人了。

1170
01:03:05.240 --> 01:03:13.140
They filled up the koi pond with water several days in advance because they had to let the chlorine evaporate from the water.
他们提前好几天就把锦鲤池注满了水，因为得让水里的氯气挥发掉。

1171
01:03:13.640 --> 01:03:16.740
They did a careful pH balance, all of that.
他们做了仔细的酸碱度平衡，诸如此类的工作。

1172
01:03:17.440 --> 01:03:19.780
Randy said the koi were very expensive.
兰迪说这些锦鲤非常昂贵。

1173
01:03:19.780 --> 01:03:28.000
And before they put the koi into the pond, they did a test with some goldfish just to make sure.
在把锦鲤放进池塘之前，他们先用几条金鱼做了测试，以确保万无一失。

1174
01:03:28.520 --> 01:03:34.740
So the goldfish, they were like, you know, when the king has a tester, eat the food firSt.
所以那些金鱼，就像你知道的，国王身边有试毒员先尝食物一样。

1175
01:03:35.040 --> 01:03:35.240
Yeah.
没错。

1176
01:03:35.920 --> 01:03:38.880
So those little goldfish, they lived.
所以那些小金鱼，它们活下来了。

1177
01:03:39.240 --> 01:03:41.160
Well, thank God they lived.
谢天谢地它们活下来了。

1178
01:03:41.480 --> 01:03:41.530
I know.
我知道。

1179
01:03:41.530 --> 01:03:43.280
The koi went in.
锦鲤被放进去了。

1180
01:03:43.540 --> 01:03:49.060
He said that we used 28 koi that were up to two feet long.
他说我们用了28条锦鲤，最长有两英尺。

1181
01:03:49.240 --> 01:03:50.560
They're very big.
它们非常大。

1182
01:03:50.760 --> 01:03:58.780
And that the total cost for the fish, the holding tanks, the pumps, the filters, and all the labor was $12,000.
鱼、储水箱、水泵、过滤器以及所有人工的总成本是12000美元。

1183
01:03:59.760 --> 01:04:02.820
Wow, that's a pricey koi pond.
哇，那可真是个昂贵的锦鲤池。

1184
01:04:03.160 --> 01:04:16.140
Well, when we started filming, Halstead shared that when they put the koi in the pond, they immediately all swam under the steps that went over the middle, you know,
嗯，当我们开始拍摄时，霍尔斯特德分享说，当他们把锦鲤放进池塘时，它们立刻全都游到了中间台阶的下面，你知道的，

1185
01:04:16.240 --> 01:04:17.080
of the koi pond.
就是锦鲤池中间的那些台阶。

1186
01:04:17.240 --> 01:04:17.780
Yeah.
是的。

1187
01:04:17.780 --> 01:04:20.560
And I guess they were in a new environment.
我想它们是到了一个新环境。

1188
01:04:20.560 --> 01:04:22.280
And so they kind of go and hide.
所以它们就躲了起来。

1189
01:04:22.480 --> 01:04:23.700
They check it out.
它们在观察环境。

1190
01:04:23.920 --> 01:04:28.380
And it takes them a bit to get comfortable and then to swim out from their hiding place.
它们需要一点时间来适应，然后才会从藏身处游出来。

1191
01:04:28.740 --> 01:04:36.680
The koi wrangler told Halstead and Warren that they had to wait for the koi to settle and come out before they could do the first take.
锦鲤管理员告诉霍尔斯特德和沃伦，他们必须等锦鲤安顿好并游出来，才能进行第一次拍摄。

1192
01:04:37.040 --> 01:04:40.180
Aw, those guys were just standing there waiting for the koi.
噢，那些人就站在那儿等着锦鲤。

1193
01:04:40.340 --> 01:04:40.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1194
01:04:40.600 --> 01:04:45.380
So someone probably made an announcement, guys, we're going to take five and let the koi get ready.
所以可能有人宣布说，伙计们，我们休息五分钟，让锦鲤准备好。

1195
01:04:46.440 --> 01:04:47.620
Waiting on the koi.
等着锦鲤呢。

1196
01:04:48.440 --> 01:04:52.140
I've got another fan question now from Nina D in Washington.
现在我还有一个来自华盛顿州妮娜·D的粉丝提问。

1197
01:04:52.700 --> 01:04:56.400
How many takes did you do of Michael falling into the pond?
迈克尔掉进池塘的那场戏你们拍了几条？

1198
01:04:57.180 --> 01:05:00.400
Randy said they really hoped the answer would be one.
兰迪说他们真的很希望答案是一条。

1199
01:05:00.820 --> 01:05:01.380
Hmm.
嗯。

1200
01:05:02.000 --> 01:05:03.940
But the answer is two.
但答案是两条。

1201
01:05:04.440 --> 01:05:05.000
Uh-oh.
糟了。

1202
01:05:05.460 --> 01:05:08.880
I think we should mention that Steve did not have a stunt double.
我觉得我们应该提一下，史蒂夫当时没有替身。

1203
01:05:09.200 --> 01:05:11.400
Steve actually fell into the pond.
史蒂夫是真的掉进了池塘里。

1204
01:05:11.640 --> 01:05:15.020
That is very clear if you go to deleted scenes.
如果你去看删减片段，这一点非常清楚。

1205
01:05:16.580 --> 01:05:25.700
When he got out from doing it the first time, they went over and they checked that sweeping camera that they had set up.
他第一次拍完爬出来的时候，他们过去检查了架设在那里的扫视摄像机。

1206
01:05:25.800 --> 01:05:27.280
To look like security footage?
是为了看起来像监控录像吗？

1207
01:05:27.280 --> 01:05:29.980
It had missed all of the action.
结果它错过了所有的动作画面。

1208
01:05:30.220 --> 01:05:30.740
Oh!
噢！

1209
01:05:31.180 --> 01:05:31.460
Oh!
噢！

1210
01:05:31.460 --> 01:05:36.960
It swept past him and then he fell and then it swept back.
镜头扫过去的时候他还没掉下去，等镜头扫回来时他已经掉进去了。

1211
01:05:36.960 --> 01:05:38.180
It missed it all.
全错过了。

1212
01:05:38.600 --> 01:05:39.000
Oh.
噢。

1213
01:05:39.200 --> 01:05:42.500
So they had to ask Steve to dry off and do it again.
所以他们不得不让史蒂夫擦干身子再拍一次。

1214
01:05:42.920 --> 01:05:53.580
Warren shared that he could tell Steve was, you know, bummed out because he had fallen into the koi pond and splashed about and now he was going to have to do it again.
沃伦分享说，他看得出史蒂夫当时很沮丧，因为他刚掉进锦鲤池里扑腾了一番，现在又得重来一遍。

1215
01:05:53.580 --> 01:05:59.300
And he said, Steve asked out loud if anyone would believe this was even possible.
他说，史蒂夫当时大声问有没有人会相信这种事真的可能发生。

1216
01:05:59.920 --> 01:06:07.180
And Paul Lieberstein, Warren's brother, who was there at the time, pointed at Warren and said, oh, it's possible.
当时也在场的沃伦的兄弟保罗·利伯斯坦指着沃伦说，噢，这确实可能发生。

1217
01:06:07.600 --> 01:06:08.440
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1218
01:06:08.440 --> 01:06:15.260
And I guess somehow up to this point, Steve was unaware that it had actually happened to Warren.
我想在那之前，史蒂夫大概一直不知道这件事真的在沃伦身上发生过。

1219
01:06:16.020 --> 01:06:20.140
And Warren said Steve just looked at him and said, wow.
沃伦说史蒂夫只是看着他，说了一句，哇。

1220
01:06:20.960 --> 01:06:29.420
Warren said that that was very generous because he could tell clearly there were many thoughts running through Steve's brain, which he chose not to say.
沃伦说那真的很宽厚，因为他能清楚地感觉到史蒂夫脑子里闪过了很多念头，但他选择了不说出来。

1221
01:06:29.420 --> 01:06:31.180
And he just said, wow.
他只是说了句，哇。

1222
01:06:31.420 --> 01:06:32.940
And then they all started laughing.
然后大家都笑了起来。

1223
01:06:33.400 --> 01:06:41.060
And Warren said, he knows a lot of people have said this, but it is true that Steve truly was the niceSt.
沃伦说，他知道很多人都这么说过，但史蒂夫确实是最友善的人，这是真的。

1224
01:06:42.440 --> 01:06:42.720
Wow.
哇。

1225
01:06:43.160 --> 01:06:47.700
Can you imagine Steve looking at you and going, wow.
你能想象史蒂夫看着你，然后说，哇，的情景吗？

1226
01:06:48.220 --> 01:06:48.820
Okay.
好吧。

1227
01:06:49.000 --> 01:06:49.780
All right.
行吧。

1228
01:06:49.940 --> 01:06:50.980
All right, then.
那就这样吧。

1229
01:06:51.240 --> 01:06:51.460
Well.
嗯。

1230
01:06:52.700 --> 01:06:58.780
Halstead shared that after Steve fell into the pond, it caused all the koi to hide again.
霍尔斯特德分享说，史蒂夫掉进池塘后，导致所有的锦鲤又躲起来了。

1231
01:06:59.420 --> 01:07:04.480
So Steve dried off, but then they had to wait for them to come out again.
所以史蒂夫擦干了身子，但他们还得等锦鲤再次游出来。

1232
01:07:05.360 --> 01:07:08.980
Halstead also shared he doesn't even think you can see any of the koi.
霍尔斯特德还说，他不觉得你能在那里面看到任何锦鲤。

1233
01:07:09.880 --> 01:07:15.460
Listen, when I watch the deleted scene, it's like black and white kind of security cam, right?
听着，我看那个删减片段的时候，那是种黑白监控摄像头的画面，对吧？

1234
01:07:15.640 --> 01:07:16.180
It's supposed to.
本该是那样的。

1235
01:07:16.480 --> 01:07:18.280
I couldn't really see the koi.
我确实没怎么看清锦鲤。

1236
01:07:18.580 --> 01:07:19.980
I don't know why I'm whispering that.
我不知道我为什么要压低声音说这个。

1237
01:07:20.120 --> 01:07:23.220
I'm doing that thing my mom does where you whisper bad news.
我这习惯跟我妈一样，说坏消息时会压低声音。

1238
01:07:23.440 --> 01:07:23.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1239
01:07:23.880 --> 01:07:25.400
I didn't see the koi.
我没看到锦鲤。

1240
01:07:26.060 --> 01:07:26.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1241
01:07:26.500 --> 01:07:31.060
Well, I guess on this second take, they did get it on the sweeping camera, but like I said,
好吧，我想在第二次拍摄时，他们确实用扫视摄像机拍到了，但就像我说的，

1242
01:07:31.180 --> 01:07:34.160
they didn't even end up using that part of the footage anyway.
反正他们最后根本没用那段素材。

1243
01:07:35.080 --> 01:07:38.840
Now, this all leads me to our final fan question about this.
现在，这一切引出了我们关于此事的最后一个粉丝提问。

1244
01:07:39.040 --> 01:07:45.180
From Logan Z in Columbus, Ohio, when everyone is watching the clip of Michael falling in
来自俄亥俄州哥伦布市的洛根·Z，当大家在电脑上观看迈克尔掉进去的片段时，

1245
01:07:45.180 --> 01:07:50.840
on the computer, did you actually get to watch the video or are you guys just pretending?
你们是真的看到了视频，还是只是在演戏？

1246
01:07:51.480 --> 01:07:53.180
It was a little bit of a combo.
算是两者结合吧。

1247
01:07:54.040 --> 01:08:00.060
So they had some of the footage of Steve falling in and they had it on a little monitor that
他们有一些史蒂夫掉进去的素材，放在一个小监视器上，

1248
01:08:00.060 --> 01:08:00.660
they showed us.
给我们看了。

1249
01:08:00.740 --> 01:08:06.120
It actually wasn't on Meredith's computer, but they did show it to the cast before we
其实那并不是在梅雷迪思的电脑上，但在我们开拍之前，

1250
01:08:06.120 --> 01:08:08.060
started rolling so we could see what happened.
他们确实给演员们看了，所以我们能看到发生了什么。

1251
01:08:09.260 --> 01:08:14.000
And then we all gather around Meredith's desk and we just sort of faked it.
然后我们都围在梅雷迪思的办公桌旁，假装在看。

1252
01:08:14.000 --> 01:08:14.900
Yes.
是的。

1253
01:08:15.220 --> 01:08:22.460
Randy said that they burned it into the computer screen with special effects, that that came
兰迪说他们是用特效把那个画面烧录进电脑屏幕里的，那是

1254
01:08:22.460 --> 01:08:22.720
later.
后来才加的。

1255
01:08:22.860 --> 01:08:28.500
And I think some of that is because they hadn't quite decided exactly what they were going
我觉得部分原因是你们拍那场戏的时候，他们还没完全决定好

1256
01:08:28.500 --> 01:08:31.720
to use yet when you guys shot your scene.
最终要用什么画面。

1257
01:08:32.620 --> 01:08:39.400
I guess we should probably explain that as they're watching this video, everyone notices
我想我们应该解释一下，大家在看这段视频时都注意到，

1258
01:08:39.400 --> 01:08:45.240
that as Michael's falling in, Jim, like, leans back.
当迈克尔掉进去的时候，吉姆往后仰了。

1259
01:08:45.880 --> 01:08:50.500
I mean, he completely, it's like he's stepping out of the way, like, no, no, no, no, no.
我是说，他完全就是一副要躲开的样子，好像在说，不，不，不，不，不。

1260
01:08:50.740 --> 01:08:52.000
Don't take me with you.
别把我带下去。

1261
01:08:52.420 --> 01:08:54.580
He does not try to grab Michael.
他根本没想去抓迈克尔。

1262
01:08:54.720 --> 01:08:56.180
He does not try to stop it.
他根本没想去阻止。

1263
01:08:56.460 --> 01:09:00.860
And everyone is now piling on Jim.
现在大家都开始指责吉姆了。

1264
01:09:00.860 --> 01:09:03.240
They're like, yeah, Jim, you could have caught Michael.
他们说，嘿，吉姆，你本可以接住迈克尔的。

1265
01:09:03.400 --> 01:09:03.980
What the hell?
搞什么鬼？

1266
01:09:04.400 --> 01:09:06.620
We got a fan question from Kelly S.
我们收到了来自缅因州波特兰市凯莉·S的一位粉丝提问，

1267
01:09:06.700 --> 01:09:11.920
in Portland, Maine, who is wondering, like, was Jim really
她想知道，迈克尔掉进锦鲤池里，

1268
01:09:11.920 --> 01:09:14.520
at fault for Michael falling in the koi pond?
真的是吉姆的错吗？

1269
01:09:14.800 --> 01:09:16.500
You know, it's not like he bumped him.
要知道，他又没撞他。

1270
01:09:17.500 --> 01:09:19.760
Kelly says, what was Jim supposed to do?
凯莉说，吉姆当时能怎么办？

1271
01:09:19.900 --> 01:09:23.000
If he'd grabbed Michael, maybe they would have both fallen in.
如果他去抓迈克尔，说不定两人都会掉进去。

1272
01:09:23.920 --> 01:09:24.400
Thoughts?
大家怎么看？

1273
01:09:25.660 --> 01:09:26.140
Thoughts.
怎么看。

1274
01:09:26.140 --> 01:09:31.140
It's sort of an interesting character assessment of your personal character.
这算是对你个人品格的一种有趣的评估。

1275
01:09:31.380 --> 01:09:34.100
It's like fight, flight, or freeze, right?
就像是战斗、逃跑或僵住反应，对吧？

1276
01:09:34.420 --> 01:09:36.640
So Michael's falling.
所以迈克尔掉下去了。

1277
01:09:36.840 --> 01:09:43.720
Let's say you and I are walking over a koi pond and you're next to me and you start to fall.
假设你和我走在锦鲤池边，你就在我旁边，然后你开始往下掉。

1278
01:09:43.720 --> 01:09:46.960
I would hope my first instinct would be to grab for you.
我希望我的第一本能是伸手去抓你。

1279
01:09:47.100 --> 01:09:48.300
I mean, I do that with my kids.
我是说，我对我的孩子们就是这样。

1280
01:09:48.300 --> 01:09:53.620
You know how that mom instinct kicks in, like, you're at a soccer game and there's a ball that
你知道那种母亲的本能是怎么触发的吗，比如你在看足球比赛，有个球

1281
01:09:53.620 --> 01:09:58.380
goes crazy towards the stands and you grab your kid out of the way?
失控飞向看台，你会一把把孩子拉开？

1282
01:09:58.640 --> 01:10:00.640
I mean, it's just like a reflex.
我是说，那纯粹是一种反射。

1283
01:10:01.020 --> 01:10:07.420
Lady, this just made me remember something that happened in my real life.
蕾迪，这让我想起我现实生活中发生的一件事。

1284
01:10:07.720 --> 01:10:07.980
What?
什么事？

1285
01:10:09.220 --> 01:10:12.640
So I'm just remembering this.
我突然想起来了。

1286
01:10:13.400 --> 01:10:20.440
I was in the kitchen and Lee walked in the kitchen and he was soaking wet, just like
当时我在厨房，李走进厨房，他浑身湿透了，就像

1287
01:10:20.440 --> 01:10:22.460
this, just like he's soaking wet.
这样，就像他浑身湿透了一样。

1288
01:10:22.660 --> 01:10:23.940
I'm like, what happened?
我问，发生什么事了？

1289
01:10:24.180 --> 01:10:24.560
I know.
我知道。

1290
01:10:24.660 --> 01:10:25.680
I know where this is going.
我知道你要说什么了。

1291
01:10:25.880 --> 01:10:26.600
What happened?
发生什么事了？

1292
01:10:26.920 --> 01:10:30.440
And he was like, I fell in the swimming pool.
他说，我掉进游泳池了。

1293
01:10:30.920 --> 01:10:32.980
I'm like, you fell in the swimming pool?
我说，你掉进游泳池了？

1294
01:10:33.180 --> 01:10:33.400
How?
怎么掉的？

1295
01:10:34.760 --> 01:10:40.940
So when our daughter was little, she used to like it when Lee would fake throw her in the
在我们女儿还小的时候，她很喜欢李假装把她扔进

1296
01:10:40.940 --> 01:10:41.600
swimming pool.
游泳池里。

1297
01:10:41.800 --> 01:10:42.100
Sure.
当然。

1298
01:10:42.260 --> 01:10:44.200
Like swing her out over and then swing her back.
就像把她荡出去，然后再荡回来。

1299
01:10:44.300 --> 01:10:44.520
Yes.
是的。

1300
01:10:44.800 --> 01:10:47.040
Swing her out over and then swing her back.
把她荡出去，然后再荡回来。

1301
01:10:47.660 --> 01:10:54.300
And he was like, I was doing the thing where I swing her over the swimming pool, but I lost
他说，我当时正把她荡在游泳池上方，但我失去了

1302
01:10:54.300 --> 01:10:56.180
my balance and I fell in.
平衡，掉进去了。

1303
01:10:56.280 --> 01:10:58.440
And I was like, is she okay?
我就问，她没事吧？

1304
01:10:58.760 --> 01:10:59.680
Did she fall in?
她掉进去了吗？

1305
01:10:59.780 --> 01:11:00.860
He's like, she's fine.
他说，她没事。

1306
01:11:01.080 --> 01:11:01.840
She's dry.
她身上是干的。

1307
01:11:02.640 --> 01:11:08.440
Well, we have a security camera, Angela, and we went and we got the footage.
安吉拉，我们有监控摄像头，我们去调了录像。

1308
01:11:08.920 --> 01:11:10.500
It is so funny.
太搞笑了。

1309
01:11:10.500 --> 01:11:12.980
We still sometimes play it as a family.
我们全家现在偶尔还会拿出来看。

1310
01:11:13.240 --> 01:11:16.920
You can see him like fake swinging her over the pool.
你能看到他假装把她荡在泳池上方。

1311
01:11:17.120 --> 01:11:22.360
He's swinging her and then he's swinging her and then he swings her and you see him start
他荡着她，又荡着她，然后他荡她的时候，你看到他开始

1312
01:11:22.360 --> 01:11:23.660
to lose his balance.
失去平衡。

1313
01:11:24.100 --> 01:11:29.620
And through some, like you're saying, like in these moments, what is your character?
就像你说的，在这些时刻，你的本性是什么？

1314
01:11:29.920 --> 01:11:31.060
What is your instinct?
你的本能是什么？

1315
01:11:32.040 --> 01:11:38.360
Through some like heroic feet, like the kind of thing you see football players do where they
通过某种英雄般的壮举，就像你看到足球运动员做的那样，他们在

